1
00:02:16,286 --> 00:02:19,405
Alps!
Put your swords up!

2
00:02:19,446 --> 00:02:22,405
We need to stand upright and strong!

3
00:02:22,566 --> 00:02:24,325
Come on!

4
00:02:24,406 --> 00:02:26,565
We stepped on the Mongolians' tail.

5
00:02:26,726 --> 00:02:30,485
They will confront us sooner or later.

6
00:02:30,686 --> 00:02:33,485
All alps needs to be trained!

7
00:02:33,686 --> 00:02:35,765
We'll take more measures.

8
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:39,927
We'll be more careful in
the border and Karacahisar

9
00:02:39,939 --> 00:02:42,725
which is the passing
route of Mongolians.

10
00:02:42,886 --> 00:02:47,605
My brother must have reached Karacahisar
with Boran Bey and Holofira by now.

11
00:02:48,046 --> 00:02:51,165
I'll inform the other border
posts about your order.

12
00:02:51,326 --> 00:02:53,085
Go ahead, son.

13
00:02:53,446 --> 00:02:57,125
Ride to Akhisar immediately with Gonca.

14
00:02:57,446 --> 00:03:00,965
We've conquered it just
recently so need to fortify it.

15
00:03:01,806 --> 00:03:03,965
While we fight Mongolians...

16
00:03:04,046 --> 00:03:08,525
...we shouldn't give the heathens any chances.

17
00:03:10,006 --> 00:03:11,845
As you order, my Bey.

18
00:03:12,286 --> 00:03:16,005
I need to go finish my preparations, my Bey.

19
00:03:16,006 --> 00:03:18,205
-Stay safe, son.
-Alright, my Bey.

20
00:03:18,206 --> 00:03:20,645
Allah is The Righteous! Allah is Eternal!

21
00:03:20,846 --> 00:03:24,885
-My Bey!
-Allah is The Righteous! Allah is Eternal!

22
00:03:24,966 --> 00:03:26,885
You said I'm no longer a groom.

23
00:03:26,966 --> 00:03:29,565
But it's an honor for
me to take care of Iltutan.

24
00:03:29,566 --> 00:03:31,525
I've just renewed his shoes.

25
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:36,805
Thanks, Ilbay.

26
00:03:36,926 --> 00:03:38,445
Thank you.

27
00:03:38,926 --> 00:03:45,725
Allah is The Righteous! Allah is Eternal!

28
00:03:46,406 --> 00:03:50,885
-Allah is The Righteous! Allah is Eternal!
-Allah is The Righteous! Allah is Eternal!

29
00:03:51,846 --> 00:03:53,405
Osman Bey.

30
00:03:53,566 --> 00:03:58,285
This hammer you hit on this
anvil for the sake of Allah..

31
00:03:58,366 --> 00:04:02,805
...is the same with the sword our
warriors hits on the chests of heathens.

32
00:04:03,286 --> 00:04:09,845
Well... You need to hit more hammers
to spread Allah's name in the whole world!

33
00:04:10,206 --> 00:04:13,765
And every man in our army
will be swinging a sword!

34
00:04:13,886 --> 00:04:16,084
As you order, my Bey!

35
00:04:16,286 --> 00:04:19,925
We will hit on the anvil until
our wrists are broken, for sure.

36
00:04:20,166 --> 00:04:22,485
Thank you, thnak you.

37
00:04:22,766 --> 00:04:24,085
My Bey.

38
00:04:25,486 --> 00:04:28,845
-Beys have joined the council.
-Okay, Samil.

39
00:04:29,366 --> 00:04:31,165
May your work be easy!

40
00:04:38,446 --> 00:04:41,805
Keep taking measures, Osman.

41
00:04:43,086 --> 00:04:47,525
We'll see if you could show
off when your plan fails!

42
00:04:54,646 --> 00:04:55,965
Aunt.

43
00:04:56,686 --> 00:04:59,045
I almost got caught, aunt.

44
00:05:04,726 --> 00:05:07,045
What's going on little bird?

45
00:05:10,206 --> 00:05:12,405
Meryem, come on.

46
00:05:23,686 --> 00:05:26,765
Meryem, are you alright?

47
00:05:27,486 --> 00:05:30,005
-Are you alright, girl?
-It's fine.

48
00:05:30,286 --> 00:05:32,565
I just lost my balance.

49
00:05:35,126 --> 00:05:37,005
I've become Fatma's friend.

50
00:05:37,406 --> 00:05:40,565
-We're closer to them now.
-Good.

51
00:05:41,686 --> 00:05:43,245
Get much closer.

52
00:05:43,806 --> 00:05:45,645
Gain their trust completely.

53
00:05:46,046 --> 00:05:47,725
It's time.

54
00:05:48,126 --> 00:05:51,325
Why am I just waiting to kill, aunt?

55
00:05:52,046 --> 00:05:54,445
Your being there is useful for me.

56
00:05:55,606 --> 00:05:58,085
Look... Thanks to you...

57
00:05:58,206 --> 00:06:02,445
...I made Mongolians
raise troubles against Kayis.

58
00:06:03,046 --> 00:06:04,485
Yes.

59
00:06:05,606 --> 00:06:06,845
You know what, aunt?

60
00:06:07,126 --> 00:06:09,485
God proved his justice.

61
00:06:10,406 --> 00:06:13,725
They took my family from me.

62
00:06:14,286 --> 00:06:16,805
And God took their daughter.

63
00:06:19,206 --> 00:06:22,325
Bala...
Bala is suffering.

64
00:06:27,046 --> 00:06:29,885
As much as I do.

65
00:06:30,126 --> 00:06:32,005
Not as much as you do.

66
00:06:32,126 --> 00:06:34,605
You have nobody.

67
00:06:34,646 --> 00:06:39,485
She has a husband and children.

68
00:06:40,086 --> 00:06:41,765
They're all with her.

69
00:06:42,406 --> 00:06:46,245
You say Orhan Bey takes measures
against the Mongols in Karacahisar...

70
00:06:46,286 --> 00:06:51,845
...while Alaeddin Bey takes measures against
the Byzantine infidels in Akhisar, my Bey.

71
00:06:52,526 --> 00:06:57,125
-Other measures will be taken, we know, but..
-But?

72
00:06:57,686 --> 00:07:02,605
-What is your concern, Begum Hatun?
-We all know what the Mongols do.

73
00:07:03,646 --> 00:07:09,205
Can we resist such a threat
by only taking precautions?

74
00:07:09,566 --> 00:07:11,085
I don't know, my Bey.

75
00:07:11,446 --> 00:07:12,965
What should we do?

76
00:07:13,126 --> 00:07:15,925
If we are facing such a trouble...

77
00:07:16,086 --> 00:07:20,605
...I say we should unite with powerful
Turkish Beylics like Germiyan and Candar...

78
00:07:21,326 --> 00:07:25,925
...and ensure unity at the frontiers, my Bey.

79
00:07:26,286 --> 00:07:28,285
What should we do, Cerkutay?

80
00:07:29,806 --> 00:07:30,925
My Bey...

81
00:07:31,966 --> 00:07:34,325
Begum Hatun surely knows that...

82
00:07:34,526 --> 00:07:39,765
...Germiyan and Candar
have bowed to the Mongols.

83
00:07:40,606 --> 00:07:41,965
In short, my Bey...

84
00:07:42,566 --> 00:07:44,645
The path Begum Hatun suggests...

85
00:07:45,126 --> 00:07:46,525
...is not the right one.

86
00:07:49,966 --> 00:07:52,525
My Bey, I agree with Cerkutay Bey.

87
00:07:52,526 --> 00:07:55,965
You are a new Bey, Saruca Bey.

88
00:07:59,166 --> 00:08:00,765
He is new...

89
00:08:01,366 --> 00:08:02,405
..but..

90
00:08:02,726 --> 00:08:05,805
..he is talented enough to see the difference...

91
00:08:06,246 --> 00:08:07,965
...between the right and wrong.

92
00:08:14,156 --> 00:08:16,915
We cannot trust those who bow to Mongols...

93
00:08:16,915 --> 00:08:19,115
...and pledge allegiance to them.

94
00:08:19,326 --> 00:08:20,485
Begum Hatun.

95
00:08:20,686 --> 00:08:24,085
If we do as you say...

96
00:08:24,566 --> 00:08:26,605
...then we will be destroyed.

97
00:08:30,966 --> 00:08:33,085
We are alone against Mongols.

98
00:08:33,525 --> 00:08:37,125
But we will always stand tall against those...

99
00:08:37,126 --> 00:08:40,565
...who set their eyes on our state and nation.

100
00:09:31,486 --> 00:09:33,205
Mongols are coming.

101
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:36,605
Their cursed feet have touched our land again.

102
00:09:39,686 --> 00:09:43,485
Fatma, come on, my daughter,
you and the others go to the tent.

103
00:10:17,126 --> 00:10:21,085
My Bey, Mongol commander Ulugan is coming.

104
00:10:21,086 --> 00:10:23,405
Didn't you notice him as he got in the tribe?

105
00:10:23,406 --> 00:10:26,125
My Bey, they suddenly
appeared in front of the tribe.

106
00:10:26,126 --> 00:10:28,205
Observer Alps didn't see them my Bey.

107
00:10:50,086 --> 00:10:53,885
As we talk about trouble,
trouble arrives at our door.

108
00:10:55,206 --> 00:10:57,085
What will we do now, Osman Bey?

109
00:10:57,246 --> 00:10:59,325
The way they came here...

110
00:11:02,326 --> 00:11:04,245
...will also be their fate.

111
00:11:55,646 --> 00:11:57,565
Osman Bey.

112
00:11:58,686 --> 00:12:00,605
Commander Ulugan.

113
00:12:01,286 --> 00:12:03,845
Don't be mad at your Alps...

114
00:12:04,566 --> 00:12:07,045
...because they couldn't notice our arrival.

115
00:12:07,046 --> 00:12:09,165
After Karesi Bey pledged allegiance...

116
00:12:09,166 --> 00:12:12,645
..we went through the
steep mountains to get here.

117
00:12:13,086 --> 00:12:14,165
Besides..

118
00:12:14,286 --> 00:12:16,285
...if we don't want it..

119
00:12:16,926 --> 00:12:18,445
...let alone you...

120
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:23,365
...even the eagle in the sky won't notice us.

121
00:12:52,566 --> 00:12:54,045
I swear by...

122
00:12:56,086 --> 00:12:57,645
...everything on the ground...

123
00:12:59,766 --> 00:13:03,285
everything between them.

124
00:13:06,566 --> 00:13:08,725
As long as you and...

125
00:13:10,446 --> 00:13:13,805
...those like you come to our lands...

126
00:13:15,286 --> 00:13:16,405
..we will..

127
00:13:17,566 --> 00:13:20,165
...always be sharp swords.

128
00:13:23,806 --> 00:13:27,325
You are always ready for battle, right, Osman?

129
00:13:30,886 --> 00:13:33,325
But I did not come here to fight...

130
00:13:34,366 --> 00:13:36,165
..I came here to meet you.

131
00:13:47,846 --> 00:13:50,325
I sent my envoy Toygar to you.

132
00:13:50,566 --> 00:13:56,205
But neither did he return, nor did
we receive any message from you.

133
00:13:57,366 --> 00:14:01,925
So I decided to come here and be Osman's guest.

134
00:14:03,046 --> 00:14:05,005
Your envoy, Toygar.

135
00:14:07,486 --> 00:14:09,525
We will talk about that matter.

136
00:14:11,326 --> 00:14:16,205
But first, tell your nokers...

137
00:14:17,526 --> 00:14:19,805
So that you came here as guests...

138
00:14:22,566 --> 00:14:25,165
...they should act accordingly.

139
00:14:28,006 --> 00:14:31,165
Or else..

140
00:14:36,846 --> 00:14:38,885
Let's go inside.

141
00:14:49,526 --> 00:14:51,045
Cerkutay.

142
00:14:53,126 --> 00:14:55,765
Ah Cerkutay.

143
00:14:56,926 --> 00:14:58,605
Now only your name and...

144
00:14:59,606 --> 00:15:02,285
...your blood is Mongol, huh?

145
00:15:51,566 --> 00:15:53,405
Who are you, stranger?

146
00:15:53,966 --> 00:15:56,285
What are you doing here alone?

147
00:16:02,246 --> 00:16:03,725
Don't you hear me?

148
00:16:03,966 --> 00:16:05,245
I am talking to you!

149
00:16:05,806 --> 00:16:07,765
Mongol trouble is at the frontiers.

150
00:16:07,766 --> 00:16:09,525
Go back to your house.

151
00:16:10,606 --> 00:16:12,485
I heard you but..

152
00:16:12,966 --> 00:16:14,365
...why should I go back?

153
00:16:15,246 --> 00:16:18,165
Does Mongols' arrival scare you, brave boy?

154
00:16:18,166 --> 00:16:20,125
I am just worried about you.

155
00:16:20,166 --> 00:16:23,445
Those miserable men will die here.

156
00:16:33,366 --> 00:16:35,565
Who will kill Mongols?

157
00:16:35,926 --> 00:16:38,565
Osman? -Yes, Osman Bey.

158
00:16:38,566 --> 00:16:41,965
Osman Bey and his valiant Alps!

159
00:16:42,446 --> 00:16:45,245
Once they show their heads, they will all die!

160
00:16:45,286 --> 00:16:47,285
You are on a lucky day, brave boy.

161
00:16:49,486 --> 00:16:51,205
Your wish came true.

162
00:17:59,726 --> 00:18:03,525
Commander Ulugan is in Osman's tribe.

163
00:18:04,406 --> 00:18:06,405
He will poison Osman's blood...

164
00:18:06,406 --> 00:18:08,845
...and make his seeing eyes blind.

165
00:18:09,086 --> 00:18:10,805
They will be relieved.

166
00:18:11,366 --> 00:18:13,925
They will think they won't face an attack.

167
00:18:14,406 --> 00:18:16,045
Then..

168
00:18:16,686 --> 00:18:20,125
...Karacahisar will be their grave.

169
00:18:21,206 --> 00:18:24,005
How will we get in there, Commander Altuga?

170
00:18:28,966 --> 00:18:35,205
When night falls, we will break
Karacahisar's defenses through the tunnels.

171
00:18:35,206 --> 00:18:37,245
They won't even sense it.

172
00:18:37,286 --> 00:18:41,005
Who did you torture to learn about
the tunnels, Commander Altuga?

173
00:18:41,086 --> 00:18:46,365
Ulugan has a skilled spy near
Osman who reveals all his weaknesses.

174
00:18:46,606 --> 00:18:50,205
This spy has now given us both Karacahisar...

175
00:18:50,406 --> 00:18:54,805
...and Shahzade Orhan's head.

176
00:19:01,526 --> 00:19:04,365
I am just like you, Osman.

177
00:19:05,046 --> 00:19:06,645
We conquered many castles...

178
00:19:07,326 --> 00:19:09,605
..and cities.

179
00:19:11,166 --> 00:19:14,285
But my tent is the only place I can be happy.

180
00:19:15,086 --> 00:19:17,245
Did you come here just to talk about this?

181
00:20:01,206 --> 00:20:03,685
First, we will drink kimiz, Osman.

182
00:20:08,606 --> 00:20:13,645
I do not become friends with
anyone who I haven't drunk kimiz with.

183
00:20:16,926 --> 00:20:19,685
Wolves can only be friends with wolves.

184
00:20:34,846 --> 00:20:37,725
When I entered your tribe, I noticed something.

185
00:20:38,086 --> 00:20:40,285
Your Alps are getting ready.

186
00:20:41,006 --> 00:20:44,205
Will you fight someone...

187
00:20:44,966 --> 00:20:46,205
...or...

188
00:20:46,926 --> 00:20:49,765
...are you expecting an attack?

189
00:20:49,766 --> 00:20:53,125
Turks live their life by
standing against the cruel...

190
00:20:53,326 --> 00:20:57,405
...as wolves live their life by killing jackals.

191
00:21:00,366 --> 00:21:03,805
We are always ready for battle. Now...

192
00:21:05,686 --> 00:21:07,605
The reason for your visit...

193
00:21:08,766 --> 00:21:10,685
..is your envoy Toyga

194
00:21:13,486 --> 00:21:15,645
I killed him with my sword.

195
00:21:18,846 --> 00:21:20,885
I cut his head off.

196
00:21:53,166 --> 00:21:54,125
So...

197
00:21:55,846 --> 00:21:59,285
...you sent Toygar to Erlik Khan, huh?

198
00:22:05,966 --> 00:22:09,445
And you bravely tell me you killed Toygar...

199
00:22:09,606 --> 00:22:13,845
...right in front of me
without hesitation, Osman?

200
00:22:19,486 --> 00:22:20,765
Cerkutay!

201
00:22:24,536 --> 00:22:26,595
Cerkutay

202
00:22:28,166 --> 00:22:31,145
Your blood still runs fast, huh?

203
00:22:39,686 --> 00:22:41,995
Karacahisar Castle

204
00:22:42,686 --> 00:22:44,605
Alps!

205
00:22:44,806 --> 00:22:49,045
You will increase the security of
Karacahisar and the roads leading to it.

206
00:22:49,446 --> 00:22:51,525
The Mongol threat is at the door.

207
00:22:51,646 --> 00:22:53,965
Lukas dog on the other side.

208
00:22:55,166 --> 00:22:59,605
At all costs, we will defend Karacahisar.

209
00:23:00,286 --> 00:23:04,725
Anyone who shows weakness
or neglects their duty...

210
00:23:05,366 --> 00:23:07,525
...will not be forgiven, know this.

211
00:23:07,526 --> 00:23:09,245
Now everyone to their duties.

212
00:23:09,246 --> 00:23:12,485
As you order my Shahzade.

213
00:23:17,886 --> 00:23:20,005
Boran Bey. -My Shahzade.

214
00:23:21,176 --> 00:23:25,385
I suggest we also increase the watchmen at
the entrances and exits of the tribe fivefold.

215
00:23:25,385 --> 00:23:28,525
-You are right my Shahzade. I'll check.
-Alright.

216
00:23:35,726 --> 00:23:36,765
Orhan.

217
00:23:37,046 --> 00:23:40,525
Let me gather the women
capable of fighting with swords.

218
00:23:40,606 --> 00:23:42,325
Let's stay alert. Besides...

219
00:23:42,326 --> 00:23:44,565
When the cruel Mongols are at our door...

220
00:23:44,566 --> 00:23:47,005
...it does not suit a Kayi
Hatun to sit and wait.

221
00:23:47,326 --> 00:23:48,725
My Holofira..

222
00:23:50,566 --> 00:23:52,645
My beautiful wife.

223
00:23:54,086 --> 00:23:56,725
Every moment, I get to know a new side of you.

224
00:23:58,086 --> 00:24:00,605
I go back to the
first day I saw you...

225
00:24:00,926 --> 00:24:05,445
...my childhood and fall in
love with you all over again.

226
00:24:06,286 --> 00:24:09,605
So your love sometimes fades, Shahzade.

227
00:24:10,446 --> 00:24:12,285
Since you fall in love again.

228
00:24:12,286 --> 00:24:17,045
Did I say that, my moon-faced
one? I said a good thing.

229
00:24:18,606 --> 00:24:21,845
It seems to me that you
want to change the subject.

230
00:24:22,286 --> 00:24:23,685
Is that so?

231
00:24:23,766 --> 00:24:27,405
It seems to me that you might be
the one wanting to change the subject.

232
00:24:29,206 --> 00:24:32,005
Tell me then, what makes you worried?

233
00:24:33,766 --> 00:24:36,365
-Nothing.
-Holofira...

234
00:24:38,286 --> 00:24:40,485
When I look into your eyes..

235
00:24:41,526 --> 00:24:44,325
..I see the concern in them.

236
00:24:45,926 --> 00:24:48,365
Come on, tell me.

237
00:24:51,446 --> 00:24:52,765
My worry is...

238
00:24:53,046 --> 00:24:56,445
...about not being able to
help you enough in your duties.

239
00:24:57,126 --> 00:24:59,165
With one glance of yours...

240
00:25:00,366 --> 00:25:03,765
...you give me the strength to
stand against the whole world.

241
00:25:05,006 --> 00:25:06,805
You've thought well.

242
00:25:07,006 --> 00:25:08,685
Prepare the women.

243
00:25:08,806 --> 00:25:11,485
We will not let those Mongol dogs pass.

244
00:25:13,406 --> 00:25:14,165
Alright.

245
00:25:21,046 --> 00:25:24,485
My little bird gave me great news, Lukas.

246
00:25:24,766 --> 00:25:28,525
She completely gained their trust.

247
00:25:28,886 --> 00:25:31,885
That means we're one
step closer to our goal, Sofia.

248
00:25:32,926 --> 00:25:35,005
Let me give you other good news.

249
00:25:35,726 --> 00:25:39,965
Ulugan has already crossed Osman's border.

250
00:25:41,606 --> 00:25:43,245
Nice.

251
00:25:44,166 --> 00:25:48,365
Osman will never survive this hell.

252
00:25:49,606 --> 00:25:53,765
While dealing with Mongolians,
he will make mistakes.

253
00:25:54,166 --> 00:25:56,685
And his mistakes will be our weapons.

254
00:25:56,846 --> 00:26:00,405
We won't go back to Bursa,
but stay here close to Osman.

255
00:26:01,886 --> 00:26:04,605
You acted impertinently in my council.

256
00:26:05,246 --> 00:26:09,525
As you were a messenger, I tolerated that.

257
00:26:10,646 --> 00:26:12,645
But oppression...

258
00:26:13,246 --> 00:26:15,685
...will never stay unreturned.

259
00:26:43,926 --> 00:26:46,325
Too much bravery...

260
00:26:47,846 --> 00:26:50,605
...will make a man captive.

261
00:27:07,086 --> 00:27:08,525
It seems...

262
00:27:09,206 --> 00:27:13,285
...that was what caused Toygar to die.

263
00:27:18,966 --> 00:27:20,885
The reason why you came here...

264
00:27:21,486 --> 00:27:22,885
You got the answer.

265
00:27:24,006 --> 00:27:27,245
What's your purpose of your stay as a guest?

266
00:27:30,566 --> 00:27:33,965
We sent Toygar as the
messenger for a reason, Osman.

267
00:27:34,726 --> 00:27:38,845
We wanted to show the
tough face of Mongolians first.

268
00:27:40,126 --> 00:27:42,925
I don't know if you're the last

269
00:27:44,206 --> 00:27:47,205
...but you aren't the first
Mongolians I have seen.

270
00:27:50,406 --> 00:27:52,405
I know, Osman.

271
00:27:53,526 --> 00:27:57,645
We came here and believed again...

272
00:27:58,006 --> 00:28:00,365
...that you won't bow against the power.

273
00:28:01,286 --> 00:28:03,605
So we want to be allies.

274
00:28:04,406 --> 00:28:07,525
Karesi, Candar, Germiyan...

275
00:28:08,006 --> 00:28:10,525
Before the ones who bow

276
00:28:11,526 --> 00:28:15,725
...we need allies who stand strong.

277
00:28:16,686 --> 00:28:19,925
What do you mean by alliance?
-We ll talk.

278
00:28:21,286 --> 00:28:23,365
But you know

279
00:28:25,126 --> 00:28:27,645
...we've come a long way.

280
00:28:28,166 --> 00:28:31,045
As you accepted us as guests here,

281
00:28:31,566 --> 00:28:34,085
...let us have some rest.

282
00:28:35,126 --> 00:28:37,165
You need to rest, huh?

283
00:28:39,046 --> 00:28:40,525
Cerkutay.

284
00:28:40,806 --> 00:28:43,485
My Bey...
-Bey...

285
00:28:45,606 --> 00:28:47,125
Take care of him.

286
00:28:47,606 --> 00:28:49,125
As you order, my Bey.

287
00:28:49,606 --> 00:28:51,525
You didn't share our kimiz.

288
00:28:52,086 --> 00:28:55,565
Let's share your food in the evening then.

289
00:28:57,086 --> 00:28:59,325
So we can keep talking.

290
00:29:13,606 --> 00:29:15,725
Dastard.

291
00:29:18,326 --> 00:29:22,365
Their intention will be revealed soon.

292
00:29:26,366 --> 00:29:28,885
Come on, hatuns.
Come on, sisters.

293
00:29:28,886 --> 00:29:30,765
We need to work faster.

294
00:29:30,886 --> 00:29:33,925
I don't want to cook those vile Mongolians.

295
00:29:34,406 --> 00:29:36,005
Calm down, Ulgen.

296
00:29:36,166 --> 00:29:38,845
Osman Bey is hosting him so we have to.

297
00:29:39,446 --> 00:29:42,005
Ulgen is right. I feel offended too.

298
00:29:42,446 --> 00:29:44,645
Those cruel people shed too much blood.

299
00:29:45,166 --> 00:29:49,885
We'll make them pay for the
blood and the food we offer.

300
00:29:50,126 --> 00:29:53,445
But not now. Now he's a guest here.

301
00:30:02,206 --> 00:30:04,965
Let those vile Mongolians eat rock!

302
00:30:05,086 --> 00:30:06,685
May Allah curse them!

303
00:30:07,006 --> 00:30:08,605
Why do you say so, mother?

304
00:30:08,646 --> 00:30:10,765
My father is a Mongolian too.

305
00:30:10,966 --> 00:30:13,045
My Allah... I didn't mean that!

306
00:30:13,686 --> 00:30:17,645
Ghazi, people like Cerkutay Bey are different.

307
00:30:17,926 --> 00:30:20,365
We curse the cruel ones.

308
00:30:20,446 --> 00:30:22,565
Those carrying stony hearts.

309
00:30:24,206 --> 00:30:25,245
You got it?

310
00:30:30,126 --> 00:30:32,565
You have mercy for everyone.

311
00:30:33,326 --> 00:30:35,325
What about my family?

312
00:30:36,926 --> 00:30:39,125
Why didn't you show mercy for them?

313
00:30:40,286 --> 00:30:42,645
We're going to have hard times.

314
00:30:42,806 --> 00:30:45,885
We'll have to deal with both
heathens and Mongolians.

315
00:30:47,326 --> 00:30:49,565
Heathens can't harm us!

316
00:30:49,726 --> 00:30:51,325
My father will protect us all.

317
00:30:51,446 --> 00:30:53,605
And kill all the heathens.

318
00:30:54,966 --> 00:30:56,965
Take this.

319
00:31:01,286 --> 00:31:03,765
-Bala Hatun?
-Yes.

320
00:31:03,766 --> 00:31:07,725
Did you kill many Byzantines?

321
00:31:10,606 --> 00:31:14,045
The war is to provide justice, girl.

322
00:31:15,486 --> 00:31:19,925
We don't swing our swords to
kill the enemy but provide justice.

323
00:31:23,366 --> 00:31:27,445
But yes, I took many Byzantine lives.

324
00:31:29,446 --> 00:31:31,565
That's what heathens deserve.

325
00:31:31,806 --> 00:31:34,245
They hurt us a lot.

326
00:31:35,006 --> 00:31:38,245
So we loomed over them like thunderbolts!

327
00:31:51,966 --> 00:31:53,605
My girl.

328
00:31:54,846 --> 00:31:58,845
Be careful. Give it to me.

329
00:32:03,806 --> 00:32:05,725
Cerkutay.

330
00:32:07,246 --> 00:32:08,925
Bey, ha?

331
00:32:09,566 --> 00:32:15,765
So you aren't Osman's hand but a
Bey who has a voice in his council, huh?

332
00:32:19,366 --> 00:32:21,685
I'm both his soldier..

333
00:32:22,646 --> 00:32:24,445
...and a Bey of his...

334
00:32:25,446 --> 00:32:28,805
...and one of a thousand
followers fighting for his cause.

335
00:32:30,326 --> 00:32:31,925
Once upon a time

336
00:32:32,566 --> 00:32:36,005
...you were a soldier of Balgay,
the mighty Mongolian commander.

337
00:32:36,766 --> 00:32:38,965
A powerful Mongolian...

338
00:32:39,526 --> 00:32:45,245
...who was bloodthirsty against Turks
and slaughtered men, women and children!

339
00:32:46,606 --> 00:32:49,085
If you walk with a dog, you are a dog.

340
00:32:53,966 --> 00:32:56,445
If you walk with a wolf, you are a wolf.

341
00:32:59,366 --> 00:33:01,205
Thank Allah...

342
00:33:01,886 --> 00:33:04,205
I've found the right path.

343
00:33:05,886 --> 00:33:07,805
I forgot my past.

344
00:33:12,446 --> 00:33:14,005
A bad dog...

345
00:33:14,886 --> 00:33:16,885
...will bring a wolf into the herd.

346
00:33:19,646 --> 00:33:21,565
You were..

347
00:33:22,486 --> 00:33:24,325
...Balgay's bad dog.

348
00:33:27,926 --> 00:33:30,525
But your brother Altuga isn't.

349
00:33:33,446 --> 00:33:40,285
His loyalty to his blood and Khan is
higher than the highest mountains.

350
00:33:42,806 --> 00:33:45,525
Altuga...

351
00:33:48,406 --> 00:33:49,885
Altuga.

352
00:33:51,646 --> 00:33:54,725
They say he is under your command.

353
00:33:56,366 --> 00:34:00,645
Is he in the frontiers with you now?

354
00:34:03,366 --> 00:34:05,165
He is.

355
00:34:07,246 --> 00:34:09,885
He came for you, Cerkutay.

356
00:34:11,806 --> 00:34:13,565
He has a duty.

357
00:34:15,045 --> 00:34:17,844
You two are going to meet soon.

358
00:34:20,005 --> 00:34:22,565
Cerkutay Bey, the tent is ready.

359
00:34:23,485 --> 00:34:25,125
Thank you.

360
00:34:25,565 --> 00:34:28,364
You go have some rest.

361
00:34:29,525 --> 00:34:31,205
Accompany them.

362
00:34:38,246 --> 00:34:40,364
What a nice horse.

363
00:34:45,286 --> 00:34:47,605
Take action immediately, Ilbay.

364
00:34:50,045 --> 00:34:51,725
Here we go.

365
00:34:58,566 --> 00:35:00,485
Byzantine is keeping silent.

366
00:35:01,206 --> 00:35:04,445
But we will stand on alert.

367
00:35:05,286 --> 00:35:09,045
-Increase the number of watchmen.
-As you order, my Shahzade.

368
00:35:09,366 --> 00:35:10,765
Thank you.

369
00:35:11,246 --> 00:35:13,525
Now everybody get to work!

370
00:35:18,886 --> 00:35:20,925
Do I have permission my Shahzade?

371
00:35:21,446 --> 00:35:22,845
Come in.

372
00:35:29,366 --> 00:35:31,925
You wanted to see me, my Shahzade?

373
00:35:33,046 --> 00:35:34,685
Kanyumaz.

374
00:35:35,446 --> 00:35:37,405
Osman Bey...

375
00:35:37,686 --> 00:35:39,685
...accepted your loyalty oath.

376
00:35:40,726 --> 00:35:44,365
Thanks to Allah. May Allah
give Osman Bey a long life.

377
00:35:45,246 --> 00:35:47,605
This is your last chance, Kanyumaz.

378
00:35:48,606 --> 00:35:51,005
Take some lessons from the past.

379
00:35:52,726 --> 00:35:56,325
From now on, Osman Bey's cause is my cause.

380
00:35:57,286 --> 00:36:00,885
I won't disappoint him,
Gonca Hatun. Don't worry.

381
00:36:02,286 --> 00:36:03,765
Get prepared.

382
00:36:03,966 --> 00:36:07,085
We'll go back to the tribe at dawn.

383
00:36:07,246 --> 00:36:10,045
As you order, my Shahzade. As you order.

384
00:36:21,766 --> 00:36:23,365
Gonca.

385
00:36:23,726 --> 00:36:26,125
You look tense.
Is there a problem?

386
00:36:28,926 --> 00:36:30,685
Mongolians.

387
00:36:31,606 --> 00:36:35,165
They've brought blood again,
Alaaddin. Too many died.

388
00:36:35,846 --> 00:36:37,965
Too many families got ruined.

389
00:36:40,126 --> 00:36:44,005
We'll make them pay for
every drop of blood, my hatun.

390
00:36:44,566 --> 00:36:46,445
Don't be upset.

391
00:36:52,246 --> 00:36:54,685
My compassionate hatun..

392
00:36:56,206 --> 00:37:00,445
We'll heal all the wounds
together, Trickster Hatun.

393
00:37:05,046 --> 00:37:07,045
Together, scholar.

394
00:37:07,606 --> 00:37:09,565
Yes.

395
00:37:16,326 --> 00:37:18,325
Take these to our tent.

396
00:37:18,526 --> 00:37:20,165
I'll help. Come on.

397
00:37:20,326 --> 00:37:22,125
Let me help too.

398
00:37:23,646 --> 00:37:26,325
Come on, daughter. Come on.

399
00:37:28,606 --> 00:37:31,725
Throw this into the water wells, Ilbay.

400
00:37:32,326 --> 00:37:36,325
Kayi people will have a
disease that they can never heal.

401
00:37:37,086 --> 00:37:39,085
Osman will be desperate.

402
00:37:39,086 --> 00:37:40,885
As you order, Commander Ulugan.

403
00:37:41,046 --> 00:37:45,645
I will destroy the whole Kayi
tribe without swinging a sword.

404
00:37:45,726 --> 00:37:47,445
Osman will be ruined.

405
00:37:47,686 --> 00:37:51,365
And you'll sit on the chair that belongs to you.

406
00:37:51,366 --> 00:37:54,765
Blood! Blood! Blood!

407
00:37:59,686 --> 00:38:02,005
Hey, man. Stop.

408
00:38:02,126 --> 00:38:04,965
-Thank you, young man.
-I can do it.

409
00:38:51,126 --> 00:38:52,645
Hey, man!

410
00:38:53,766 --> 00:38:55,325
Here.

411
00:38:56,406 --> 00:38:57,925
Stop, man.

412
00:38:58,646 --> 00:39:01,485
I said I'd bring water to
you. Why did you bother?

413
00:39:01,726 --> 00:39:03,005
Thank you.

414
00:39:03,166 --> 00:39:06,805
-Well... I fill, you carry.
-Alright.

415
00:39:07,606 --> 00:39:10,165
Have a nice day, man.

416
00:39:31,766 --> 00:39:36,085
The uninvited will sit on the ground, they say.

417
00:39:37,286 --> 00:39:42,285
But you are a host worthy of his name.

418
00:39:45,926 --> 00:39:47,805
Enjoy it.

419
00:39:49,966 --> 00:39:52,045
Fresh meat.

420
00:39:52,326 --> 00:39:54,045
A bay horse.

421
00:39:54,286 --> 00:39:56,445
A solid sword.

422
00:39:56,726 --> 00:39:58,685
What else a man would want?

423
00:39:59,126 --> 00:40:01,685
Faith and conscience.

424
00:40:04,366 --> 00:40:09,165
Well, of course a human needs these.

425
00:40:10,806 --> 00:40:15,005
But we have another matter now.

426
00:40:18,686 --> 00:40:22,205
You mentioned alliance.
What do you mean by that?

427
00:40:22,766 --> 00:40:24,965
What do you want from me?

428
00:40:27,486 --> 00:40:33,325
A new age is beginning not only in the world
but also in the frontiers you settled in.

429
00:40:34,126 --> 00:40:41,605
You know... Karesi, Candar and all the
beys in the frontiers were subject to us.

430
00:40:44,246 --> 00:40:46,365
All of them except you.

431
00:40:48,166 --> 00:40:50,485
You know my answer.

432
00:40:51,006 --> 00:40:54,965
I'm not here for a loyalty
oath but for alliance.

433
00:40:55,566 --> 00:41:01,005
Although you aren't under our command,
you won't stand against us either.

434
00:41:02,286 --> 00:41:04,325
I told you before.

435
00:41:06,806 --> 00:41:10,085
Turks have no friends but Turks.

436
00:41:13,326 --> 00:41:15,325
Speaking of friends,

437
00:41:15,926 --> 00:41:19,805
...you weren't lucky about Turks either.

438
00:41:23,806 --> 00:41:25,405
Karesi.

439
00:41:25,606 --> 00:41:27,445
Candar, Germiyan...

440
00:41:27,806 --> 00:41:32,725
They weren't soft against you. But
against us Mongolians, they were.

441
00:41:33,046 --> 00:41:35,005
It's the same for Mongolians!

442
00:41:37,246 --> 00:41:39,165
You're divided into a thousand!

443
00:41:39,406 --> 00:41:40,925
From north to south.

444
00:41:41,206 --> 00:41:43,285
From south to east.

445
00:41:45,926 --> 00:41:49,165
You got broken into many khanates.

446
00:41:50,086 --> 00:41:56,565
Now you mention alliance for
those who you couldn't make bow?

447
00:41:59,246 --> 00:42:06,285
Or are you gathering strength for your
Khan to provide the unity of Mongolians?

448
00:42:07,766 --> 00:42:09,725
You're arrogant, Osman.

449
00:42:10,526 --> 00:42:14,605
Do you doubt our strength?

450
00:42:16,086 --> 00:42:22,645
We don't want you to stay
alone in your lands in the frontiers.

451
00:42:23,166 --> 00:42:24,805
And stay without allies.

452
00:42:24,846 --> 00:42:30,205
Besides, you shouldn't
underestimate Olcaytu Khan.

453
00:42:30,966 --> 00:42:34,165
His strength can shake the world.

454
00:42:36,446 --> 00:42:40,285
He's reached the frontiers.

455
00:42:40,686 --> 00:42:44,405
If he reaches out, he can
take any lands he wants.

456
00:42:44,886 --> 00:42:47,925
All the lands and castles.

457
00:42:54,526 --> 00:42:57,525
Karacahisar Castle

458
00:43:28,006 --> 00:43:29,085
Nokers!

459
00:43:49,446 --> 00:43:51,165
Be quiet, hide.

460
00:43:55,566 --> 00:43:56,925
What's happening here?

461
00:43:56,926 --> 00:43:58,885
Come here, open the door.

462
00:44:13,726 --> 00:44:16,565
Nokers, water the stones of Karacahisar...

463
00:44:16,566 --> 00:44:19,365
..with Turkish blood.

464
00:44:22,286 --> 00:44:23,805
They sneaked in!

465
00:44:39,326 --> 00:44:40,965
Genghis Khan...

466
00:44:42,446 --> 00:44:45,325
...before revealing his move to the enemy...

467
00:44:46,206 --> 00:44:50,925
...made his merchants his spies
and sent them upon his enemies.

468
00:44:52,486 --> 00:44:56,325
This is the lineage of Genghis,
my Shahzade. Always the same.

469
00:44:56,446 --> 00:44:59,205
Merchants, the traitors.

470
00:45:00,926 --> 00:45:03,485
They wander around the frontiers freely.

471
00:45:03,806 --> 00:45:05,045
Right.

472
00:45:05,686 --> 00:45:08,325
Right. These Mongols...

473
00:45:08,606 --> 00:45:11,525
...must have already
learned about our precautions.

474
00:45:12,526 --> 00:45:15,285
Surely, they'll look for our weakness.

475
00:45:15,846 --> 00:45:21,045
-Their spies.
-Orhan. Orhan, what happened?

476
00:45:22,086 --> 00:45:25,325
The Mongols have infiltrated the fortress.
-How? How?

477
00:45:25,326 --> 00:45:26,685
From where?

478
00:45:27,566 --> 00:45:30,325
They must have crossed through the tunnels.

479
00:45:30,486 --> 00:45:32,445
Their traitor spies...

480
00:45:32,926 --> 00:45:35,845
...fulfilled their duties.
-Orhan.

481
00:45:36,206 --> 00:45:37,685
They are getting close.

482
00:45:37,926 --> 00:45:39,725
They're coming for you.

483
00:45:40,046 --> 00:45:41,725
Let them come.

484
00:45:42,806 --> 00:45:46,645
Karacahisar will be their grave. Alps...

485
00:45:46,646 --> 00:45:50,805
...position yourselves in the south immediately.
-As you command, my Shahzade.

486
00:45:51,326 --> 00:45:53,325
We'll block their way..

487
00:45:53,926 --> 00:45:55,965
...and trap them inside the fortress.

488
00:45:57,366 --> 00:45:58,485
Boran Bey.

489
00:45:58,486 --> 00:46:00,405
Your path is my path, my Shahzade.

490
00:46:01,606 --> 00:46:05,565
-Let's kill all these dogs.
-Okay.

491
00:46:05,646 --> 00:46:09,165
-Holofira, you stay here.
-No.

492
00:46:10,326 --> 00:46:15,285
If my sword won't be drawn with yours in this
difficult time, then when will it, Orhan?

493
00:46:18,766 --> 00:46:21,485
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate. Come on.

494
00:46:33,166 --> 00:46:34,485
Nokers!

495
00:46:34,646 --> 00:46:37,165
Show the strength of Mongols to Turks!

496
00:46:37,166 --> 00:46:39,965
Spread the flames of fear in their hearts.

497
00:46:40,486 --> 00:46:41,725
Turks..

498
00:46:42,406 --> 00:46:44,005
...believe in Allah.

499
00:46:44,526 --> 00:46:45,965
They seek refuge in Him...

500
00:46:45,966 --> 00:46:49,725
...and fear only Him. You
came here without permission.

501
00:46:50,126 --> 00:46:51,485
Karacahisar..

502
00:46:51,886 --> 00:46:56,565
...will be the grave for you and your dogs.
-Orhan...

503
00:46:57,486 --> 00:46:59,405
..you must be Orhan.

504
00:46:59,526 --> 00:47:01,605
I will hold your leash..

505
00:47:02,206 --> 00:47:05,445
...and make you my dog, Orhan.
-That leash...

506
00:47:06,326 --> 00:47:09,525
...will be your execution rope, dog.

507
00:47:09,646 --> 00:47:11,965
That treacherous Cerkutay...

508
00:47:11,966 --> 00:47:13,805
...hasn't taught you the might...

509
00:47:14,286 --> 00:47:17,245
...and reputation of the Mongols, huh?

510
00:47:17,326 --> 00:47:20,845
What do you even know about
Cerkutay, you son of a dog?

511
00:47:21,526 --> 00:47:23,565
The sword you see here..

512
00:47:23,766 --> 00:47:25,845
...was made by him.

513
00:47:27,886 --> 00:47:29,125
Tell me.

514
00:47:29,446 --> 00:47:30,805
Who are you?

515
00:47:31,846 --> 00:47:33,365
Cerkutay's...

516
00:47:33,486 --> 00:47:35,325
..eternal enemy.

517
00:47:36,126 --> 00:47:38,165
His own brother.

518
00:47:40,566 --> 00:47:43,485
-Altuga.
-Altuga.

519
00:47:43,846 --> 00:47:45,685
You are correct, brave boy.

520
00:47:46,246 --> 00:47:48,605
From the barking dog at your gate...

521
00:47:48,646 --> 00:47:52,845
...to the one who dares to say a
thing, I will kill them all with my sword.

522
00:47:53,726 --> 00:47:57,525
-Nokers, attack!
-Alps! Come on!

523
00:48:26,926 --> 00:48:29,525
The southern side has fallen, my Shahzade.

524
00:48:32,766 --> 00:48:35,765
Orhan, Karacahisar is falling,
what are we going to do?

525
00:48:37,726 --> 00:48:40,765
Karacahisar won't fall before I drop my sword!

526
00:48:44,086 --> 00:48:47,165
Alps, retreat inside the fortress!

527
00:48:47,286 --> 00:48:50,005
They're escaping, catch them!

528
00:48:50,006 --> 00:48:52,165
Those who give up easily...

529
00:48:54,686 --> 00:48:57,725
...are those who earn easily.

530
00:48:58,166 --> 00:49:02,965
We suffered so much and made
many sacrifices for these lands.

531
00:49:05,606 --> 00:49:07,005
And if someone...

532
00:49:08,766 --> 00:49:11,205
...is going to set their eyes on them...

533
00:49:12,846 --> 00:49:15,125
...they will have to pay a heavy price.

534
00:49:45,086 --> 00:49:47,125
You face..

535
00:49:47,126 --> 00:49:49,845
...what's written in your destiny.

536
00:49:50,926 --> 00:49:54,445
One day, everyone pays a price.

537
00:50:03,006 --> 00:50:04,925
You hosted us well.

538
00:50:05,926 --> 00:50:07,885
We wish to host you as well.

539
00:50:07,886 --> 00:50:09,845
Where will you host us?

540
00:50:11,206 --> 00:50:14,245
-Is your tent nearby? -No.

541
00:50:14,526 --> 00:50:16,325
We are not around here.

542
00:50:16,486 --> 00:50:19,245
For now.

543
00:50:22,966 --> 00:50:25,525
But those days are not far away.

544
00:50:32,726 --> 00:50:36,125
Commander Ulugan, the
news we awaited has arrived.

545
00:50:55,526 --> 00:50:57,005
You heard, Osman.

546
00:50:58,406 --> 00:51:00,565
Our visit ends here.

547
00:51:01,646 --> 00:51:03,565
Think well on what I've said.

548
00:51:04,126 --> 00:51:06,085
We will meet again.

549
00:51:06,846 --> 00:51:09,485
Don't forget my words.

550
00:51:10,206 --> 00:51:11,485
Ulugan.

551
00:51:15,886 --> 00:51:17,165
Because..

552
00:51:19,246 --> 00:51:20,925
...I always do as I say.

553
00:51:27,126 --> 00:51:29,885
Cerkutay. -My Bey.

554
00:51:30,286 --> 00:51:31,525
Come on.

555
00:51:33,366 --> 00:51:34,965
Accompany them.

556
00:51:38,566 --> 00:51:40,205
As you order, my Bey.

557
00:51:49,206 --> 00:51:51,365
Samil. -My Bey.

558
00:51:52,686 --> 00:51:54,085
Call Ilbay here.

559
00:51:54,406 --> 00:51:55,845
As you order my Bey.

560
00:52:03,406 --> 00:52:07,565
Osman Bey hosted this Mongol, but I am afraid.

561
00:52:07,566 --> 00:52:09,925
Osman Bey does not trust him either.

562
00:52:11,166 --> 00:52:13,845
Let's see what will come out of this visit.

563
00:52:15,806 --> 00:52:17,765
Can I come in, Begum Hatun?

564
00:52:28,326 --> 00:52:30,005
Come in, Ilbay Bey.

565
00:52:36,406 --> 00:52:39,085
-What happened?
-I went to the well...

566
00:52:39,606 --> 00:52:41,165
...and I brought more water.

567
00:52:43,126 --> 00:52:46,325
The water was polluted
during the last sandstorm.

568
00:52:46,926 --> 00:52:48,605
You can now drink clean water.

569
00:52:51,566 --> 00:52:53,005
Thank you.

570
00:52:55,726 --> 00:52:57,085
But..

571
00:52:57,806 --> 00:53:00,925
Do you visit every tent
with that jug in your hand?

572
00:53:01,126 --> 00:53:03,525
Or is this care special to me?

573
00:53:12,286 --> 00:53:13,685
Good night.

574
00:53:23,446 --> 00:53:24,565
What happeend?

575
00:53:25,126 --> 00:53:28,365
Why did Ilbay come here at this hour?
-Nothing important.

576
00:53:28,646 --> 00:53:30,045
He brought water.

577
00:53:30,446 --> 00:53:31,845
He brought water.

578
00:53:38,766 --> 00:53:41,245
Boran Bey, come. Come. Come on Alps!

579
00:53:42,566 --> 00:53:44,485
They are here, Commander Altuga!

580
00:53:44,526 --> 00:53:47,125
Open the door then, what are you waiting for?

581
00:53:48,846 --> 00:53:50,085
Holofira.

582
00:53:51,246 --> 00:53:52,485
Holofira.

583
00:53:53,446 --> 00:53:55,325
Nokers, break the doors!

584
00:53:57,286 --> 00:54:00,605
There is a tunnel behind
the throne. Go through there.

585
00:54:00,606 --> 00:54:03,045
No, no, I won't leave. You
know I won't leave you here.

586
00:54:03,046 --> 00:54:06,965
Holofira. There is no other way. You have to go!
-I won't leave you here!

587
00:54:07,126 --> 00:54:10,565
I will stay here! -Come!

588
00:54:11,046 --> 00:54:13,605
-Orhan! I said no!
-I cannot let you stay here!

589
00:54:15,306 --> 00:54:17,405
Where will you run, Orhan?

590
00:54:17,446 --> 00:54:19,925
Hang on brothers... Come on.

591
00:54:20,046 --> 00:54:24,205
Holofira. Holofira. Don't be scared.

592
00:54:24,206 --> 00:54:27,565
Nothing will happen to me.
-But what if something happens to you?

593
00:54:27,646 --> 00:54:29,685
What am I going to do then?
-Holofira.

594
00:54:29,686 --> 00:54:32,045
I promise you, nothing will happen to me.

595
00:54:32,046 --> 00:54:36,525
You will go and tell my father
everything that happened here. Alright?

596
00:54:36,886 --> 00:54:40,245
This tunnel will lead
you to the Kartalini region.

597
00:54:40,246 --> 00:54:42,565
You'll leave without even looking back.

598
00:54:45,446 --> 00:54:46,645
Come.

599
00:54:50,686 --> 00:54:53,485
My Shahzade, the door will break. Come on!

600
00:54:54,366 --> 00:54:56,725
I will take you, Orhan!

601
00:55:00,926 --> 00:55:03,885
In the name of Allah.

602
00:55:08,766 --> 00:55:11,165
Come, you dastard dogs, come!

603
00:55:29,206 --> 00:55:32,565
I will break your arrogance
courage with my sword, Orhan.

604
00:55:32,566 --> 00:55:36,125
But my sword will get rid of your
courage along with your head.

605
00:55:36,326 --> 00:55:39,374
Your tongue that dares
to speak brave words will...

606
00:55:39,386 --> 00:55:42,445
...beg for mercy when you
fall into my hands, Orhan.

607
00:55:54,416 --> 00:55:56,085
Now it's your turn.

608
00:55:56,886 --> 00:55:59,325
Bring them.

609
00:56:08,006 --> 00:56:11,165
The last two men left in your fortress, Orhan.

610
00:56:11,526 --> 00:56:15,485
You should be thankful, Ulugan wants you alive.

611
00:56:21,326 --> 00:56:22,685
Nokers.

612
00:56:23,766 --> 00:56:25,605
Take their swords.

613
00:56:29,526 --> 00:56:31,405
Ah Cerkutay ah.

614
00:56:33,766 --> 00:56:35,765
Mindless Cerkutay.

615
00:56:37,366 --> 00:56:44,125
Look at the Turks you offered
loyalty after betraying the Mongols.

616
00:56:51,446 --> 00:56:57,685
You will answer for all the innocents
and martyrs who you hurt with your sword!

617
00:56:57,686 --> 00:56:59,205
For all of them!

618
00:56:59,806 --> 00:57:07,525
Nokers, throw these long-tongued,
weak handed men into the dungeon.

619
00:57:08,086 --> 00:57:11,125
Ulugan will take care of them tomorrow.

620
00:57:29,646 --> 00:57:30,405
What?

621
00:57:30,826 --> 00:57:33,365
What do you mean you have a brother, Cerkutay?

622
00:57:33,366 --> 00:57:36,805
Am I not your wife? How
could you hide this from me?

623
00:57:38,526 --> 00:57:40,085
I couldn't tell you, my wife.

624
00:57:41,566 --> 00:57:42,845
I didn't say it...

625
00:57:43,526 --> 00:57:45,085
..to anyone.

626
00:57:47,246 --> 00:57:48,685
How could I know..

627
00:57:48,686 --> 00:57:51,285
...one day they would come to the frontiers?

628
00:57:51,286 --> 00:57:54,125
They came to the frontiers by hurting others.

629
00:57:56,566 --> 00:57:58,125
What is this brother's name?

630
00:57:59,006 --> 00:58:02,805
-Altuga.
-Altuga. Is he your enemy?

631
00:58:03,126 --> 00:58:05,365
In their eyes, I am a traitor.

632
00:58:05,606 --> 00:58:07,205
He must be my enemy.

633
00:58:08,076 --> 00:58:11,125
Can a brother ever be an enemy
to his brother? That's not possible.

634
00:58:11,125 --> 00:58:13,125
You should see him first, then we'll know.

635
00:58:13,206 --> 00:58:14,805
He is not, he cannot be.

636
00:58:15,046 --> 00:58:17,885
You should go and talk to him. What?

637
00:58:18,246 --> 00:58:20,645
I have an uncle?

638
00:58:21,926 --> 00:58:22,965
No!

639
00:58:24,486 --> 00:58:26,565
Father, does he also use double swords?

640
00:58:26,566 --> 00:58:28,085
Does he look like you or me?

641
00:58:29,006 --> 00:58:31,925
Did you start eavesdropping?!

642
00:58:33,206 --> 00:58:34,925
Father, who does he resemble?

643
00:58:35,406 --> 00:58:39,285
Son, it's been a long time. I...

644
00:58:40,966 --> 00:58:43,245
..don't know who he looks like...

645
00:58:44,606 --> 00:58:46,245
Or what kind of person he is..

646
00:58:47,446 --> 00:58:49,245
Is he as strong as you?

647
00:58:49,806 --> 00:58:52,005
Come on! I am hungry!

648
00:58:52,006 --> 00:58:53,885
Come on, look.

649
00:58:55,126 --> 00:58:57,525
Look what I've made for you.

650
00:58:57,886 --> 00:58:59,285
Who should I give the most?

651
00:59:01,946 --> 00:59:04,499
Give it to me. Hatun, give it
to me. Don't let Ghazi grow...

652
00:59:04,499 --> 00:59:06,815
...bigger and stronger. It's
enough for him. Give it to me.

653
00:59:06,815 --> 00:59:10,245
No, mother. I will go to
battle. I will grow. No, father.

654
00:59:10,246 --> 00:59:12,525
Mother, give it to me.
-No. I made a decision.

655
00:59:12,526 --> 00:59:14,125
I work the most in the tribe.

656
00:59:14,126 --> 00:59:15,154
I will eat the most.

657
00:59:15,166 --> 00:59:16,725
-No, I will eat.
-No, mother.

658
00:59:16,726 --> 00:59:19,645
-Give it to me. -No. I will eat.
-Father, I will eat.

659
00:59:19,646 --> 00:59:23,005
No. I will eat. I will eat.

660
00:59:32,206 --> 00:59:34,725
Let go! Dastard demons!

661
00:59:34,726 --> 00:59:37,125
I swear we will make you pay for this!

662
00:59:37,126 --> 00:59:38,965
Let go! Let go!

663
00:59:57,366 --> 00:59:59,405
Shahzade.

664
01:00:02,646 --> 01:00:05,565
You are still talking.

665
01:00:06,646 --> 01:00:11,045
You and Boran are in our hands.

666
01:00:12,926 --> 01:00:15,725
I will destroy each one of you.

667
01:00:16,166 --> 01:00:19,205
You won't be able to do anything.

668
01:00:19,206 --> 01:00:23,325
Just as we killed those
before you, we will send you...

669
01:00:26,446 --> 01:00:29,285
We will send all of you to hell.

670
01:00:29,286 --> 01:00:31,765
We will send you all to hell!

671
01:00:31,766 --> 01:00:33,645
To hell!

672
01:00:43,606 --> 01:00:46,245
If it wasn't for my great commander Ulugan...

673
01:00:46,646 --> 01:00:48,925
..I would kill you know.

674
01:00:49,246 --> 01:00:50,565
But no.

675
01:00:51,206 --> 01:00:54,725
I will make you suffer worse than death, Orhan.

676
01:00:55,486 --> 01:00:59,245
Both you and Boran.

677
01:01:06,966 --> 01:01:10,405
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

678
01:01:12,726 --> 01:01:13,965
My Shahzade.

679
01:01:13,966 --> 01:01:16,485
Dastard dog.

680
01:01:16,486 --> 01:01:18,005
Come at me!

681
01:01:26,086 --> 01:01:27,085
Keep hitting!

682
01:01:34,446 --> 01:01:37,285
He came to our tribe, called himself a guest...

683
01:01:37,286 --> 01:01:40,085
...and even offered an alliance, is that so?

684
01:01:40,766 --> 01:01:42,005
Yes.

685
01:01:43,286 --> 01:01:44,605
Right.

686
01:01:46,206 --> 01:01:48,685
We took the head of his envoy.

687
01:01:49,486 --> 01:01:52,125
Yet he still stands before us and play games.

688
01:01:55,406 --> 01:01:56,525
Then...

689
01:01:56,526 --> 01:01:59,965
...what is the actual
purpose of that dog Ulugan?

690
01:02:01,166 --> 01:02:04,565
Could you notice something?

691
01:02:04,566 --> 01:02:06,525
He revealed nothing.

692
01:02:07,126 --> 01:02:08,325
Only...

693
01:02:09,126 --> 01:02:13,445
...one of his soldiers came and said they
received the news they were waiting for.

694
01:02:17,286 --> 01:02:20,725
-Can I come in, my Bey?
-Come in, Ilbay.

695
01:02:23,726 --> 01:02:24,765
My Bey...

696
01:02:25,246 --> 01:02:27,525
...I went after the Mongols as you ordered.

697
01:02:28,126 --> 01:02:30,725
But I lost them after a while.

698
01:02:34,526 --> 01:02:35,565
My Bey...

699
01:02:38,646 --> 01:02:40,485
..couldn't tell anyone but..

700
01:02:44,086 --> 01:02:45,805
..I have a brother.

701
01:02:46,846 --> 01:02:48,045
Altuga.

702
01:02:54,686 --> 01:02:56,605
Do you have a brother?

703
01:02:58,286 --> 01:02:59,445
Yes my Bey...

704
01:03:03,246 --> 01:03:04,365
Uluga

705
01:03:05,126 --> 01:03:06,925
...said that my brother Altuga...

706
01:03:07,086 --> 01:03:09,845
...was on duty at the frontiers.

707
01:03:10,486 --> 01:03:12,845
He was probably the one who sent the news.

708
01:03:13,126 --> 01:03:14,965
But I don't know what they are...

709
01:03:15,526 --> 01:03:19,605
...doing. -We will learn.

710
01:03:21,886 --> 01:03:24,965
We will learn everything. Samil.

711
01:03:28,606 --> 01:03:30,125
Yes my Bey.

712
01:03:30,126 --> 01:03:31,765
Send messengers everywhere...

713
01:03:31,766 --> 01:03:33,725
...to all our properties!

714
01:03:33,766 --> 01:03:37,565
Orhan Bey and Alaeddin Bey will
come back to the tribe immediately.

715
01:03:37,566 --> 01:03:39,045
Send someone to Akhisar.

716
01:03:39,046 --> 01:03:42,085
And you will go to Karacahisar.

717
01:03:42,686 --> 01:03:44,205
As you order, my Bey.

718
01:03:51,686 --> 01:03:54,805
-Mother, father.
-My daughter.

719
01:03:54,966 --> 01:03:56,325
Do you want some water?

720
01:03:56,326 --> 01:03:58,725
Sisters have just brought water from the well.

721
01:03:58,726 --> 01:04:00,485
Yes, give some water, my daughter.

722
01:04:00,726 --> 01:04:01,965
Thank you.

723
01:04:02,966 --> 01:04:04,005
Thank you.

724
01:04:34,326 --> 01:04:36,525
Thank you, my daughter.

725
01:04:46,846 --> 01:04:53,005
Tomorrow we will witness closely what
is happening in Osman's lands. But...

726
01:04:53,446 --> 01:04:56,725
...the thing I don't like about this is...

727
01:04:57,246 --> 01:05:00,405
...wearing stupid Turkmen clothes.

728
01:05:10,646 --> 01:05:11,685
Here.

729
01:05:11,886 --> 01:05:13,365
This is for you.

730
01:05:23,606 --> 01:05:30,525
I will do everything to end Osman and make
Great Rome strong in these lands again.

731
01:05:31,006 --> 01:05:34,525
Once the Mongols attack them...

732
01:05:34,766 --> 01:05:38,085
.we will be there to take action.

733
01:05:41,366 --> 01:05:46,685
Lukas, our soldiers will be ready at all times.

734
01:05:48,726 --> 01:05:52,405
The soldiers have already
taken their positions, Sofia.

735
01:05:53,246 --> 01:05:56,005
There will be nowhere left for Osman to escape.

736
01:06:13,846 --> 01:06:16,445
Well well, Ghazi Bey is also here.

737
01:06:20,126 --> 01:06:24,365
What would our Bey like for
breakfast? I can bring some milk.

738
01:06:24,526 --> 01:06:26,925
Honey and cream? What would you like?

739
01:06:27,886 --> 01:06:30,085
Leave me alone, mother.

740
01:06:30,086 --> 01:06:32,965
I am not feeling well today.

741
01:06:33,926 --> 01:06:37,325
Don't you have anything to do?
Why are you annoying me here?

742
01:06:37,326 --> 01:06:39,165
Go and cook food.

743
01:06:39,206 --> 01:06:41,685
Work with the Sisters. Go on.

744
01:06:45,646 --> 01:06:48,645
I didn't say anything, my Hatun! He did!

745
01:06:48,846 --> 01:06:51,685
He learned all these things from you!

746
01:06:52,486 --> 01:06:54,085
I will kill you now!

747
01:06:54,406 --> 01:06:56,005
I will kill you know! Who...

748
01:06:56,006 --> 01:06:58,725
How dare you talk to your mother like this?

749
01:06:58,726 --> 01:07:02,045
Let me! Annoying you? Did you hear
him? Did you grow up and become a man?

750
01:07:02,046 --> 01:07:03,525
Cerkutay, let go!

751
01:07:03,526 --> 01:07:05,565
I swear, I will break your bones.

752
01:07:05,566 --> 01:07:08,685
Help!

753
01:07:11,246 --> 01:07:13,805
-What's going on?
-Osman Bey!

754
01:07:15,126 --> 01:07:18,325
Osman Bey! Father!

755
01:07:22,366 --> 01:07:26,845
-Father. Father... What happened, girl?

756
01:07:27,286 --> 01:07:30,005
Mongolians attacked Karacahisar.

757
01:07:39,246 --> 01:07:41,685
Orhan... Orhan?

758
01:07:41,806 --> 01:07:44,885
Orhan and Boran Bey stayed to defend the castle.

759
01:07:45,046 --> 01:07:47,645
Orhan sent me here to inform you.

760
01:07:55,846 --> 01:07:58,005
Uluga

761
01:08:02,846 --> 01:08:05,085
This is Ulugan's doing.

762
01:08:06,806 --> 01:08:11,205
He stalled us in the tribe
and then attacked Karacahisar.

763
01:08:14,086 --> 01:08:17,045
Cerkutay, Ilbay! Bring the horses!

764
01:08:21,446 --> 01:08:23,365
My Bey, I'll go with you.

765
01:08:23,645 --> 01:08:27,325
Alaaddin must be on the way.
He will take care of the tribe.

766
01:08:28,406 --> 01:08:30,245
Alright, Bala. Let's go.

767
01:08:32,446 --> 01:08:35,045
Mother. Mother.

768
01:08:35,326 --> 01:08:38,484
No, Holofira. Stand strong.

769
01:08:38,725 --> 01:08:40,845
Orhan will be alright. Don't worry.

770
01:08:41,206 --> 01:08:43,205
Nothing will happen to him.

771
01:09:11,606 --> 01:09:13,925
What's wrong with me?

772
01:09:26,645 --> 01:09:28,765
Boran Bey.

773
01:09:29,246 --> 01:09:31,325
Boran Bey. Boran Bey.

774
01:09:35,765 --> 01:09:37,885
Are you alright, Boran Bey?

775
01:09:38,286 --> 01:09:40,524
Don't worry, my Shahzade.

776
01:09:41,246 --> 01:09:44,165
I'm good enough to beat
those dogs, thank Allah.

777
01:09:44,286 --> 01:09:48,365
When we reach the headquarters,
you won't have no strength left.

778
01:09:49,166 --> 01:09:51,005
You vile dog.

779
01:09:51,526 --> 01:09:54,085
Wolf's sharper look than a sword..

780
01:09:54,366 --> 01:09:58,485
...is enough to spread fear in the
jackal's heart, you Mongolian dog.

781
01:09:59,406 --> 01:10:01,285
Orhan.

782
01:10:02,486 --> 01:10:04,685
This is your lucky day.

783
01:10:07,086 --> 01:10:11,365
Ulugan wants you alive and healthy.

784
01:10:12,366 --> 01:10:14,005
Otherwise...

785
01:10:14,926 --> 01:10:18,045
...I would have taken your eyes out by now.

786
01:10:18,686 --> 01:10:21,485
While you have a chance, you aren't doing it.

787
01:10:21,846 --> 01:10:24,245
But when I get you

788
01:10:24,846 --> 01:10:28,285
...I will make you regret this.

789
01:10:30,606 --> 01:10:32,845
I got your leash, Orhan.

790
01:10:33,646 --> 01:10:37,605
I can tighten it or put it around your neck.

791
01:10:37,766 --> 01:10:41,525
But you will witness.

792
01:10:42,566 --> 01:10:46,007
You will see what happens
to Osman who has established a...

793
01:10:46,019 --> 01:10:49,605
...state with a few alps and
rebelled against Mongolians.

794
01:10:53,966 --> 01:10:56,365
With those a few alps,

795
01:10:57,566 --> 01:10:59,845
...we will break Mongolian dominance...

796
01:11:00,286 --> 01:11:03,125
...and raise our sanjak all around the world!

797
01:11:03,846 --> 01:11:06,525
We'll glorify Allah's name more...

798
01:11:07,246 --> 01:11:09,925
...and bring peace to the whole world.

799
01:11:10,006 --> 01:11:13,805
-Allah is the greatest!
-You're brain dead, Orhan.

800
01:11:14,766 --> 01:11:16,845
Brain dead.

801
01:11:18,086 --> 01:11:22,525
Mongolians will water the lands with blood.

802
01:11:23,006 --> 01:11:26,845
And they will make your people kneel with blood.

803
01:11:28,326 --> 01:11:30,845
I will cut off your wriggling head.

804
01:11:31,326 --> 01:11:33,125
You should know this.

805
01:11:33,566 --> 01:11:36,645
..in these lands which bear fearless men,

806
01:11:37,006 --> 01:11:40,245
...we're never afraid of death.

807
01:11:40,566 --> 01:11:45,805
We bow against nobody.
We seek mercy from nobody.

808
01:11:46,606 --> 01:11:49,765
I will make you seek mercy.

809
01:11:49,926 --> 01:11:52,605
-We will see. -Nokers!

810
01:11:53,246 --> 01:11:55,645
Ulugan is waiting. Take them!

811
01:11:55,766 --> 01:12:00,765
I swear on my name that I
will kill you with your nokers.

812
01:12:17,566 --> 01:12:21,965
Mongolians caught Shahzade Orhan. That's awful!

813
01:12:29,046 --> 01:12:32,805
It's alright, dear. It's alright.

814
01:12:33,006 --> 01:12:36,125
-It's alright, baby.
-Sisters.

815
01:12:42,166 --> 01:12:44,405
How long has it been like this, Fatma?

816
01:12:44,486 --> 01:12:46,565
Everybody got sick at the same time?

817
01:12:46,646 --> 01:12:50,805
Fever, nausea and
stomachache since this morning.

818
01:12:51,246 --> 01:12:53,445
Especially elders and children.

819
01:12:53,646 --> 01:12:56,405
All troubles come one after another!

820
01:12:56,526 --> 01:13:00,845
Everybody got sick here and
Mongolians caught Orhan Bey.

821
01:13:02,566 --> 01:13:04,725
Father will come back with Orhan.

822
01:13:05,126 --> 01:13:08,725
And we'll take care of people
during their absence, right?

823
01:13:25,376 --> 01:13:27,285
Peace be upon you.

824
01:13:27,846 --> 01:13:30,525
Holofira, you are back.

825
01:13:33,486 --> 01:13:34,805
My brother?

826
01:13:37,286 --> 01:13:38,885
What's the matter?

827
01:13:38,926 --> 01:13:40,365
What's wrong with people?

828
01:13:40,606 --> 01:13:43,045
Brother, bad things are happening.

829
01:13:43,246 --> 01:13:45,205
Mongolians attacked Karacahisar.

830
01:13:45,326 --> 01:13:47,845
They caught Orhan and Boran Bey.

831
01:13:48,086 --> 01:13:50,165
We don't know how they are doing.

832
01:13:50,566 --> 01:13:52,645
What are you saying?

833
01:13:53,246 --> 01:13:55,565
Father has gone to Karacahisar.

834
01:13:56,126 --> 01:14:00,045
-He'll come back with Orhan.
-I will go join him.

835
01:14:01,406 --> 01:14:03,925
-Come on.
-Holofira.

836
01:14:05,046 --> 01:14:07,805
Guldane! Guldane!

837
01:14:08,646 --> 01:14:10,085
Help!

838
01:14:10,206 --> 01:14:12,845
-Guldane? Sisters!
-What's going on?

839
01:14:16,766 --> 01:14:20,205
-What's going on here?
-She's not well.

840
01:14:21,206 --> 01:14:24,085
-She has high fever.
-She's burning.

841
01:14:24,166 --> 01:14:26,245
Alps, bring a stretcher!

842
01:14:29,166 --> 01:14:32,565
Take her to the healing
house! Come on, hurry up!

843
01:14:32,686 --> 01:14:35,365
-Come on, help! Hold it!
-Come on.

844
01:14:35,966 --> 01:14:40,125
Come on, come on.
-Careful.

845
01:14:40,446 --> 01:14:44,685
-Come on, take her to the healing house quickly!
-Here we go.

846
01:14:45,166 --> 01:14:47,045
I won't leave you
alone, brother.

847
01:14:47,566 --> 01:14:49,645
Alaaddin, Alaaddin.

848
01:14:49,806 --> 01:14:52,525
Children and elders are falling down one by one.

849
01:14:52,566 --> 01:14:54,645
This looks like a terrible pandemic.

850
01:14:54,886 --> 01:14:56,645
We need you here.

851
01:15:05,816 --> 01:15:07,365
Samil.

852
01:15:08,206 --> 01:15:11,605
-What's the situation?
-It's not good, my Bey.

853
01:15:11,766 --> 01:15:14,685
Mongolians captured the castle.

854
01:15:16,526 --> 01:15:19,045
What about Boran and Orhan?

855
01:15:19,286 --> 01:15:21,725
Going to the castle, we heard from people...

856
01:15:21,926 --> 01:15:25,485
Nokers took Orhan Bey and Boran away.

857
01:15:29,846 --> 01:15:31,765
Ulugan.

858
01:15:31,926 --> 01:15:34,325
What evil are you up to?

859
01:15:34,486 --> 01:15:36,045
Where did they took them?

860
01:15:36,366 --> 01:15:39,765
It's said they took them to the north
but we don't know where, my Bey.

861
01:15:40,286 --> 01:15:43,165
But they said they didn't seem to be well.

862
01:15:43,486 --> 01:15:47,045
Orhan Bey and Boran were being tortured.

863
01:15:52,206 --> 01:15:53,765
Samil.

864
01:15:53,966 --> 01:15:56,565
Go to the south with your alps.

865
01:15:57,206 --> 01:15:59,765
-Saruca and Yusuf. -My Bey. - My Bey.

866
01:16:00,086 --> 01:16:02,285
You go that way.

867
01:16:03,406 --> 01:16:05,645
And we go to the north.

868
01:16:05,766 --> 01:16:08,125
Look everywhere. Come on, my warriors!

869
01:16:08,486 --> 01:16:11,325
-As you order, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

870
01:16:30,766 --> 01:16:32,605
Bala.

871
01:16:34,806 --> 01:16:38,605
-Are you alright?
-I'm fine, my Bey.

872
01:16:41,726 --> 01:16:45,685
-You're burning. Are you alright?
-It's good.

873
01:16:45,966 --> 01:16:48,205
Fine.
Fine.

874
01:16:52,046 --> 01:16:56,485
I will destroy the whole Kayi
tribe without swinging a sword.

875
01:16:56,686 --> 01:17:01,365
Osman will be ruined. And you'll
sit on the chair that belongs to you.

876
01:17:02,846 --> 01:17:07,245
Come on. We can't stop
until we take Orhan and Boran.

877
01:17:07,446 --> 01:17:09,925
We will shake the world if we have to.

878
01:17:12,926 --> 01:17:15,005
Come on, warriors!

879
01:17:31,926 --> 01:17:34,365
We've found them, Lukas.

880
01:17:35,046 --> 01:17:39,325
They're outnumbered. It's
time to beat Osman, Sofia.

881
01:17:39,646 --> 01:17:43,445
We'll choke them at their weakest moment.

882
01:17:44,926 --> 01:17:46,445
Lukas.

883
01:17:47,006 --> 01:17:49,245
-Let's go after them.
-Alright.

884
01:18:34,326 --> 01:18:36,005
The flames..

885
01:18:36,926 --> 01:18:39,205
...shall guide you, Ulugan.

886
01:18:42,286 --> 01:18:44,045
Red blood..

887
01:18:44,606 --> 01:18:47,445
...shall give you life, Ulugan.

888
01:18:49,326 --> 01:18:53,645
Your enemies shall vanish, Ulugan!

889
01:19:23,406 --> 01:19:30,725
These lands where we fight,
take lives and shed blood...

890
01:19:30,886 --> 01:19:32,165
...shall glorify us!

891
01:19:38,086 --> 01:19:41,405
May Tengri be our witness!

892
01:19:42,606 --> 01:19:45,445
We'll spread our kin in the whole world!

893
01:20:08,086 --> 01:20:11,285
I've brought you a gift, Ulugan.

894
01:20:22,606 --> 01:20:25,405
Salute Altuga, who is back with victory.

895
01:20:25,526 --> 01:20:29,805
Altuga! Altuga! Altuga!

896
01:20:53,046 --> 01:20:55,485
You poor creatures.

897
01:20:56,206 --> 01:21:00,525
You kneel in front of me miserably.

898
01:21:02,046 --> 01:21:04,805
You can't stand against mighty Mongolians.

899
01:21:05,286 --> 01:21:09,845
I'll take all your cities and lands from you.

900
01:21:10,006 --> 01:21:13,325
I will make you my dogs!

901
01:21:13,606 --> 01:21:15,805
I will take a bath in your blood.

902
01:21:17,566 --> 01:21:19,725
You vile dog.

903
01:21:20,886 --> 01:21:25,605
Untie my hands if you have courage.

904
01:21:26,326 --> 01:21:32,045
Then we will see who can make the other his dog!

905
01:21:32,246 --> 01:21:35,805
Come on! Do you have courage? Untie me!

906
01:21:36,006 --> 01:21:38,365
I will put out your fire, Orhan.

907
01:21:38,886 --> 01:21:42,205
I will destroy your father and Kayi.

908
01:21:43,126 --> 01:21:45,285
My Shahzade!

909
01:21:50,286 --> 01:21:54,045
You dastard. Kill us now..

910
01:21:54,366 --> 01:21:56,085
...or untie our hands.

911
01:21:56,206 --> 01:21:59,445
Let's see who wins.

912
01:22:00,406 --> 01:22:06,085
Ulugan never takes lives without games.

913
01:22:07,286 --> 01:22:09,805
Your torture isn't over yet.

914
01:22:12,206 --> 01:22:14,445
Tie them and take them away.

915
01:22:15,566 --> 01:22:21,165
We ll kill all of you! All
of you! Dog! You vile dog!

916
01:22:22,406 --> 01:22:24,365
You vile dog!

917
01:22:40,246 --> 01:22:42,085
Take care of her.

918
01:22:52,926 --> 01:22:55,765
Let me check. Let me check.

919
01:22:57,406 --> 01:23:00,045
Alaaddin Bey. Yaren..

920
01:23:01,246 --> 01:23:03,365
-Wait, wait.
-Alaaddin Bey.

921
01:23:03,606 --> 01:23:04,925
I'm here.

922
01:23:07,686 --> 01:23:09,645
Help us, my Allah.

923
01:23:09,806 --> 01:23:12,085
Is this a pandemic, Alaaddin Bey?

924
01:23:13,246 --> 01:23:14,285
No.

925
01:23:15,766 --> 01:23:17,845
Not a pandemic.

926
01:23:18,846 --> 01:23:20,965
It's poison.

927
01:23:22,966 --> 01:23:25,765
Everybody is infected at the same time...

928
01:23:26,286 --> 01:23:27,965
Something they eat or drink.

929
01:23:28,006 --> 01:23:30,205
Not everyone cooks the same food.

930
01:23:30,926 --> 01:23:33,325
You're right, Meryem.

931
01:23:34,366 --> 01:23:37,085
Something everybody reaches at the same time.

932
01:23:37,606 --> 01:23:38,725
Water.

933
01:23:38,926 --> 01:23:41,805
Water! Move aside, sister!

934
01:23:43,286 --> 01:23:45,645
Who would poison the well and why?

935
01:24:00,526 --> 01:24:02,885
Vile dogs!

936
01:24:04,566 --> 01:24:06,845
They put poison in the water.

937
01:24:07,206 --> 01:24:09,565
Dastards.

938
01:24:10,606 --> 01:24:12,245
Alps

939
01:24:14,846 --> 01:24:18,725
Examine the water well immediately and clean it!

940
01:24:19,246 --> 01:24:23,205
For now, fetch water from the well in the woods.

941
01:24:23,246 --> 01:24:26,365
Until that water comes
here, nobody will drink water!

942
01:24:26,366 --> 01:24:27,965
Come on.

943
01:24:31,086 --> 01:24:32,525
My Shahzade.

944
01:24:33,166 --> 01:24:35,725
We all drank water from there.

945
01:24:42,406 --> 01:24:44,845
What poison, Alaaddin?

946
01:24:46,726 --> 01:24:49,325
Some poison I have never seen before.

947
01:24:49,566 --> 01:24:51,445
I don't know what it is.

948
01:24:52,166 --> 01:24:54,485
But Mongolians did this.

949
01:24:57,126 --> 01:25:00,685
We need oak bark and
sarsaparilla root immediately.

950
01:25:00,846 --> 01:25:03,053
How can we find
them in this season?

951
01:25:03,065 --> 01:25:03,805
We have to.

952
01:25:04,246 --> 01:25:06,245
We have to. Fatma.

953
01:25:08,286 --> 01:25:10,565
All of you may be poisoned.

954
01:25:11,126 --> 01:25:14,965
Boil yellow centaury and make
everyone drink it. You drink it too.

955
01:25:15,126 --> 01:25:18,125
It will decrease the
poison's effect, God willing.

956
01:25:18,366 --> 01:25:20,245
-We'll do it now, my Bey.
-Good.

957
01:25:20,246 --> 01:25:21,925
-Kanyumaz.
-My Bey.

958
01:25:21,926 --> 01:25:24,685
Demand reinforcements from Sogut immediately.

959
01:25:24,686 --> 01:25:27,805
Alps drank water too. We
shouldn't fall weak here.

960
01:25:27,846 --> 01:25:29,685
As you order, my Bey.

961
01:25:30,126 --> 01:25:34,005
-Gonca, let's go. May Allah protect you.
-Alright.

962
01:25:34,126 --> 01:25:35,925
-Come on.
-I'm going too.

963
01:25:38,326 --> 01:25:40,485
We can find them faster.

964
01:25:45,566 --> 01:25:49,285
Fine. Come on, come on.

965
01:25:59,926 --> 01:26:01,685
You don't look well.

966
01:26:02,006 --> 01:26:04,325
Are you poisoned too?

967
01:26:04,846 --> 01:26:08,365
I'm fine, Meryem.

968
01:26:09,326 --> 01:26:12,085
Don't be afraid. I will be alright.

969
01:26:13,126 --> 01:26:16,365
We need to find clean water. Come on.

970
01:26:24,326 --> 01:26:26,325
Bala Hatun.. Bala?

971
01:26:27,846 --> 01:26:29,765
Bala.

972
01:26:31,326 --> 01:26:34,285
Bala. What's wrong with you?

973
01:26:36,646 --> 01:26:39,525
I don't feel well, Osman.

974
01:26:41,326 --> 01:26:45,205
Something's wrong with
me too. I'm not well, my Bey.

975
01:26:48,526 --> 01:26:51,645
-The same here, my Bey.
-You too?

976
01:27:10,966 --> 01:27:13,085
This is Ulugan's doing.

977
01:27:15,126 --> 01:27:18,125
He must have put poison
in the water in our tribe.

978
01:27:21,006 --> 01:27:24,845
But I don't know how he could do
it while there were so many alps.

979
01:27:28,646 --> 01:27:31,245
Everybody in the tribe got poisoned then.

980
01:27:31,766 --> 01:27:35,205
Alaaddin is there. He will find a cure.

981
01:27:37,086 --> 01:27:40,125
Yes, let's find Orhan first.

982
01:27:41,926 --> 01:27:44,485
Come on!

983
01:27:46,766 --> 01:27:48,285
Osman!

984
01:27:55,806 --> 01:27:58,525
I brought your death to you.

985
01:28:00,526 --> 01:28:02,445
Red demon..

986
01:28:05,806 --> 01:28:08,325
I was waiting for you to come out.

987
01:28:19,406 --> 01:28:21,445
It's time for revenge, Osman.

988
01:28:25,806 --> 01:28:27,645
We have more men than you do.

989
01:28:29,526 --> 01:28:32,685
You will die alone here.

990
01:28:42,126 --> 01:28:44,325
Is that so?

991
01:28:44,326 --> 01:28:46,565
Cerkutay. -My Bey.

992
01:28:50,766 --> 01:28:52,805
We will break through here.

993
01:28:52,806 --> 01:28:54,485
As you order my Bey.

994
01:28:56,406 --> 01:28:58,805
There is still time for these dastards.

995
01:29:00,126 --> 01:29:01,725
We are going to Orhan.

996
01:29:02,006 --> 01:29:03,725
Come on!

997
01:29:05,686 --> 01:29:07,485
Ya Allah!

998
01:29:17,646 --> 01:29:19,805
Soldiers! Run!

999
01:29:24,086 --> 01:29:25,405
Catch them!

1000
01:29:30,366 --> 01:29:34,405
Osman would never escape even if
he knew he was going to die, Lukas!

1001
01:29:35,926 --> 01:29:38,525
There is something else behind this.

1002
01:30:38,446 --> 01:30:40,925
Holy Shaman, what do you see?

1003
01:31:02,006 --> 01:31:04,325
I see a gray Sky Wolf.

1004
01:31:04,446 --> 01:31:07,365
It has the world in his claw.

1005
01:31:08,366 --> 01:31:11,405
Thousands follow him.

1006
01:31:16,246 --> 01:31:20,285
They are the descendants of the
ones who melted the iron mountain.

1007
01:31:20,686 --> 01:31:22,325
He is a dark man.

1008
01:31:26,046 --> 01:31:27,245
Who is he?

1009
01:31:41,806 --> 01:31:43,005
Osman!

1010
01:31:50,246 --> 01:31:52,565
..Osman does not die..

1011
01:31:53,766 --> 01:31:56,085
...he and his descendants...

1012
01:31:56,366 --> 01:32:00,925
..will ride horses on three continents
and seven regions. They will spread.

1013
01:32:00,926 --> 01:32:03,165
Osman's name will be known everywhere.

1014
01:32:03,446 --> 01:32:07,285
Osman's reputation will
be spoken of in the world.

1015
01:32:12,566 --> 01:32:15,125
The Sky Wolf is Osman, Ulugan.

1016
01:32:45,126 --> 01:32:48,685
As long as...

1017
01:32:48,686 --> 01:32:50,445
...I live...

1018
01:32:51,286 --> 01:32:54,165
..I will never allow this.

1019
01:32:56,806 --> 01:32:58,845
First, I will take his honor...

1020
01:33:00,166 --> 01:33:02,205
..then his life.

1021
01:33:04,366 --> 01:33:09,845
You will die at my feet, Osman.

1022
01:33:24,126 --> 01:33:26,805
Cerkutay. -My Bey.

1023
01:33:26,806 --> 01:33:28,325
My Bey

1024
01:33:28,766 --> 01:33:30,045
Cerkutay.

1025
01:33:36,126 --> 01:33:37,525
Cerkutay.

1026
01:33:37,566 --> 01:33:38,845
My Bey

1027
01:33:38,846 --> 01:33:39,885
Are you alright?

1028
01:33:44,006 --> 01:33:46,445
My Bey, they are getting close!

1029
01:33:51,046 --> 01:33:51,805
Ilbay.

1030
01:33:51,806 --> 01:33:54,205
Take the horses and continue from here.

1031
01:33:54,206 --> 01:33:57,005
We need to confuse them.
We will meet in the north.

1032
01:33:57,006 --> 01:34:00,245
As you order, my Bey.

1033
01:34:00,246 --> 01:34:02,685
Come on, get up.
Come on, get up.

1034
01:34:02,966 --> 01:34:04,925
Let's go.

1035
01:34:04,926 --> 01:34:06,605
Come on.

1036
01:34:22,326 --> 01:34:24,325
There is no trace anywhere.

1037
01:34:24,326 --> 01:34:26,285
What are we going to do now, my Bey?

1038
01:34:40,246 --> 01:34:42,205
Wait... Allah is Great.

1039
01:34:42,206 --> 01:34:45,765
He will show us a way for sure.

1040
01:34:47,286 --> 01:34:48,885
Let's go this way.

1041
01:34:48,886 --> 01:34:50,605
Come on.

1042
01:35:07,166 --> 01:35:09,285
If the rope that ties my hands...

1043
01:35:09,806 --> 01:35:13,565
...was my execution rope,
I would not feel ashamed.

1044
01:35:14,206 --> 01:35:17,605
But falling into the hands of these dogs and...

1045
01:35:17,606 --> 01:35:20,605
...putting Osman Bey in a difficult situation...

1046
01:35:22,086 --> 01:35:25,885
Now is not the time for shame..

1047
01:35:26,366 --> 01:35:30,005
...but the time to rise and ruin
the games of these dastard dogs.

1048
01:35:30,806 --> 01:35:32,605
Okay my Shahzade.

1049
01:35:33,046 --> 01:35:35,245
We will escape from here.

1050
01:35:36,366 --> 01:35:38,645
My Shahzade. -Tell me.

1051
01:35:39,606 --> 01:35:42,245
There is a dagger in my boot.

1052
01:35:42,886 --> 01:35:48,925
But I cannot find a chance
to reach and take it. But...

1053
01:35:49,606 --> 01:35:54,445
...they have defenses here
that is like an eagle's nest.

1054
01:35:57,086 --> 01:35:58,325
You...

1055
01:35:58,566 --> 01:36:00,405
..stretch out your boot.

1056
01:36:28,206 --> 01:36:30,005
Eagles do not fit in cages...

1057
01:36:31,286 --> 01:36:32,645
..lions...

1058
01:36:33,206 --> 01:36:35,765
...do not fit in forests, Boran Bey.

1059
01:36:51,486 --> 01:36:53,325
What are you doing there?

1060
01:36:55,726 --> 01:36:57,205
What is in your hand?

1061
01:36:57,206 --> 01:36:59,325
In my hand..

1062
01:37:00,286 --> 01:37:03,005
...in my hand...

1063
01:37:05,206 --> 01:37:07,285
...is your death.

1064
01:37:39,806 --> 01:37:42,525
My Shahzade, I will distract them, you leave!

1065
01:37:42,526 --> 01:37:46,683
We either leave together, or
we die together, Boran Bey.

1066
01:37:46,695 --> 01:37:48,085
My Shahzade.

1067
01:37:48,366 --> 01:37:50,485
Come on, come on.

1068
01:38:03,006 --> 01:38:05,565
So you are running, dogs.

1069
01:38:05,686 --> 01:38:10,965
You are trying to escape but
no one escapes from Ulugan.

1070
01:38:10,966 --> 01:38:12,405
Orhan.

1071
01:38:12,406 --> 01:38:14,085
If you have the courage..

1072
01:38:14,686 --> 01:38:18,605
...if you trust your strength, face me.

1073
01:38:18,606 --> 01:38:21,525
Come and I will take that dirty head of yours.

1074
01:38:22,446 --> 01:38:24,205
Step aside.

1075
01:38:34,366 --> 01:38:35,565
Altuga.

1076
01:38:37,926 --> 01:38:39,685
Bring them here.

1077
01:38:40,006 --> 01:38:42,725
I will show them what pain is.

1078
01:38:45,166 --> 01:38:47,325
You and I will meet again Orhan.

1079
01:38:47,326 --> 01:38:49,525
You are lucky today, Altuga.

1080
01:38:49,926 --> 01:38:51,685
You are lucky today.

1081
01:38:52,326 --> 01:38:53,805
Bring them.

1082
01:39:19,686 --> 01:39:20,805
God..

1083
01:39:23,086 --> 01:39:24,645
Protect him...

1084
01:39:25,406 --> 01:39:27,485
Do not take him from me.

1085
01:39:35,646 --> 01:39:37,885
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

1086
01:39:38,086 --> 01:39:40,925
Allah is sufficient for us.

1087
01:39:40,966 --> 01:39:42,925
You protected him before.

1088
01:39:44,206 --> 01:39:47,565
Now I am asking You with his heart.

1089
01:39:47,566 --> 01:39:50,965
I am begging You with his words.

1090
01:39:53,846 --> 01:39:56,605
Please, protect him.

1091
01:40:43,526 --> 01:40:46,565
My Bey, what did these dastards make us drink?

1092
01:40:47,046 --> 01:40:49,325
We are slowly losing our strength.

1093
01:41:00,246 --> 01:41:02,445
I don't know what made us drink...

1094
01:41:03,246 --> 01:41:07,405
...but once its effect disappears...

1095
01:41:07,486 --> 01:41:10,085
...we know what to do to them.

1096
01:41:13,806 --> 01:41:15,885
My Bey. My Bey.

1097
01:41:21,126 --> 01:41:21,845
My Bey.

1098
01:41:22,046 --> 01:41:24,285
I tried hard, but I couldn't succeed.

1099
01:41:24,326 --> 01:41:26,765
They are everywhere. They are coming here.

1100
01:41:26,766 --> 01:41:29,605
I can smell you, Osman.

1101
01:41:29,606 --> 01:41:31,365
The red devil is here.

1102
01:41:34,006 --> 01:41:35,765
Come here.

1103
01:41:36,846 --> 01:41:39,925
Come here, come here.

1104
01:41:51,606 --> 01:41:53,285
Come face me.

1105
01:41:53,966 --> 01:41:56,485
Let's end this today, Osman.

1106
01:42:04,366 --> 01:42:06,205
Where are you?

1107
01:42:08,886 --> 01:42:11,325
My Bey, don't. Please don't.

1108
01:42:11,486 --> 01:42:15,285
My Bey, we shouldn't face them in this state.

1109
01:42:18,886 --> 01:42:21,805
Cerkutay.

1110
01:42:36,286 --> 01:42:37,485
Are you alright?

1111
01:42:38,446 --> 01:42:39,565
I am.

1112
01:42:40,006 --> 01:42:41,205
You are not.

1113
01:42:43,686 --> 01:42:45,365
You are worried about Orhan.

1114
01:42:45,646 --> 01:42:47,485
Do you think I can't see it?

1115
01:42:48,166 --> 01:42:51,285
You are trying to stand tall, I know.

1116
01:42:51,606 --> 01:42:54,245
But your heart is in pain, I'm aware.

1117
01:42:55,886 --> 01:42:57,405
I cannot fall, Gonca.

1118
01:42:58,406 --> 01:43:02,205
I cannot show my pain to
anyone who cannot heal it.

1119
01:43:03,926 --> 01:43:05,125
Holofira.

1120
01:43:07,166 --> 01:43:09,285
No matter what we went through...

1121
01:43:09,326 --> 01:43:11,285
No matter what..

1122
01:43:11,726 --> 01:43:13,925
You are not alone in this situation.

1123
01:43:14,726 --> 01:43:18,285
If you get tired, I will help you.

1124
01:43:23,166 --> 01:43:25,805
And when you gain your strength again...

1125
01:43:26,446 --> 01:43:29,005
...if you want to see me against you again...

1126
01:43:30,166 --> 01:43:31,485
...don't worry.

1127
01:43:32,006 --> 01:43:33,605
I'll stand against you.

1128
01:43:34,166 --> 01:43:36,325
Then we can fight.

1129
01:43:48,086 --> 01:43:51,085
No. No! It's no where!

1130
01:43:51,326 --> 01:43:52,965
It's not here!

1131
01:43:54,366 --> 01:43:56,525
What are we going to do Alaeddin?

1132
01:43:58,766 --> 01:44:00,605
Let's go that side.

1133
01:44:00,646 --> 01:44:02,365
We don't have much time, come on.

1134
01:44:02,806 --> 01:44:03,965
Come on.

1135
01:44:12,446 --> 01:44:14,045
We never bow down to..

1136
01:44:14,566 --> 01:44:16,525
...the dishonest ones!

1137
01:44:16,606 --> 01:44:19,045
Do your best, you dog!

1138
01:44:19,726 --> 01:44:21,405
Dastard dogs!

1139
01:44:39,286 --> 01:44:42,285
You don't know Ulugan yet.

1140
01:44:43,446 --> 01:44:45,725
You will experience pain now.

1141
01:44:48,846 --> 01:44:53,925
The most valuable trait of the
Alps is the hands that hold swords.

1142
01:44:57,166 --> 01:45:01,565
If you can't hold a sword, you'll die, Orhan.

1143
01:45:02,246 --> 01:45:03,485
You'll die.

1144
01:45:20,966 --> 01:45:23,685
Watch, you dog.

1145
01:45:30,606 --> 01:45:32,045
Altuga.

1146
01:45:44,646 --> 01:45:46,045
My Shahzade.

1147
01:45:47,086 --> 01:45:49,485
Kayis could not hear you, Orhan!

1148
01:45:49,686 --> 01:45:51,405
Louder!

1149
01:45:55,046 --> 01:45:58,085
Has your fire gone out, Orhan?

1150
01:45:59,406 --> 01:46:02,005
Has your tail, held high, now bent?

1151
01:46:06,006 --> 01:46:10,845
If you try to escape again,
I'll nail your other hand too.

1152
01:46:11,486 --> 01:46:13,805
I told you, you'll be a dog at my door.

1153
01:46:14,206 --> 01:46:16,525
No one escapes from Ulugan.

1154
01:46:17,086 --> 01:46:22,165
Your greatest regret in this
life will be not killing me, dog

1155
01:46:22,166 --> 01:46:24,125
Not killing me!

1156
01:46:29,406 --> 01:46:31,285
Crush the miserable Boran.

1157
01:46:31,446 --> 01:46:33,205
Bury him in the ground.

1158
01:46:33,206 --> 01:46:37,125
Come, come, you dog's children, come.

1159
01:46:42,286 --> 01:46:44,725
I swear, Ulugan!

1160
01:46:45,366 --> 01:46:50,045
I swear, I will take your life! I swear!

1161
01:47:17,846 --> 01:47:20,325
I found you, Osman.

1162
01:47:44,126 --> 01:47:47,805
Who dares attack the
commander and soldiers of Rome?

1163
01:47:48,206 --> 01:47:52,085
Holy Ulugan calls you. You will come with me.

1164
01:47:57,486 --> 01:47:59,485
The infidels are uniting again.

1165
01:47:59,926 --> 01:48:02,725
But we know how to defeat them.

1166
01:48:07,566 --> 01:48:09,725
Get lost Mongol.

1167
01:48:10,246 --> 01:48:13,525
Osman is in my hands, I will kill him.

1168
01:48:13,606 --> 01:48:15,885
I will not repeat it, Hatun.

1169
01:48:17,206 --> 01:48:19,645
You will either listen to me, or...

1170
01:48:19,646 --> 01:48:23,525
I hope Ulugan has a good thing to give to us...

1171
01:48:23,526 --> 01:48:25,685
Or else, it will be really, really bad.

1172
01:48:26,526 --> 01:48:27,725
We are leaving.

1173
01:48:36,846 --> 01:48:39,925
My Bey, what are we going to do now?

1174
01:48:40,326 --> 01:48:45,085
You will follow them. We will find Ulugan's
place. That's what matters the most for us.

1175
01:48:45,086 --> 01:48:47,365
As you order, my Bey.

1176
01:48:53,766 --> 01:48:55,445
Bala.

1177
01:49:10,006 --> 01:49:11,325
Alaeddin.

1178
01:49:12,166 --> 01:49:14,725
Alaeddin, is it this one?

1179
01:49:15,766 --> 01:49:19,725
No. Not this one. -What about this?

1180
01:49:22,006 --> 01:49:23,325
It looks like this one.

1181
01:49:23,366 --> 01:49:25,325
But this is not what we need either.

1182
01:49:25,326 --> 01:49:28,205
But I guess we are close.

1183
01:49:28,206 --> 01:49:31,005
We will search thoroughly. Come on. Come on.

1184
01:49:39,926 --> 01:49:41,125
Hamza Alp.

1185
01:49:42,246 --> 01:49:43,605
What are you doing here?

1186
01:49:43,606 --> 01:49:46,485
Alaeddin Bey, I lost my mother.

1187
01:49:46,926 --> 01:49:52,005
I came to do whatever I can
so other families will not suffer.

1188
01:49:53,806 --> 01:49:55,405
May Allah have mercy on her.

1189
01:49:56,326 --> 01:50:00,125
Yeter Mother was a mother to
all of us. I'm sorry for your loss.

1190
01:50:01,406 --> 01:50:02,445
But..

1191
01:50:03,486 --> 01:50:07,085
...I know that as long as
she has a son like you...

1192
01:50:07,446 --> 01:50:09,325
...her deed book will always be open...

1193
01:50:09,366 --> 01:50:11,873
...and it will be filled with
good deeds, God willing.

1194
01:50:11,885 --> 01:50:12,725
God willing.

1195
01:50:12,726 --> 01:50:14,165
Come on then.

1196
01:50:14,206 --> 01:50:18,525
Help us. -As you order my Shahzade.
-Come on.

1197
01:50:27,446 --> 01:50:28,725
Alaeddin.

1198
01:50:29,366 --> 01:50:31,845
I found it! -Yes!

1199
01:50:32,486 --> 01:50:33,925
This is the one!

1200
01:50:34,606 --> 01:50:35,885
Thanks to Allah!

1201
01:50:40,366 --> 01:50:42,365
Cannibal dogs!

1202
01:51:23,006 --> 01:51:25,005
Gonca, Holofira. Are you alright?

1203
01:51:25,046 --> 01:51:27,645
-Yes. Are you?
-Thanks to Allah, I'm good.

1204
01:51:28,806 --> 01:51:31,605
But there is no sarsaparilla here.

1205
01:51:31,726 --> 01:51:33,205
We're running out of time.

1206
01:51:33,326 --> 01:51:34,885
Let's pick these roots.

1207
01:51:34,926 --> 01:51:38,005
-I'll try to make antidote with them.
-Let's go.

1208
01:51:38,766 --> 01:51:40,165
Come on.

1209
01:51:44,326 --> 01:51:49,485
Hold on. Obviously, his
intention isn't to kill us...

1210
01:51:49,726 --> 01:51:51,685
...but make us live.

1211
01:51:52,206 --> 01:51:54,525
He's playing with us, Osman.

1212
01:51:55,486 --> 01:51:58,245
-My Bey.
-Cerkutay.

1213
01:52:00,806 --> 01:52:03,405
My Bey, they are moving too fast.

1214
01:52:03,886 --> 01:52:05,605
We lost the trails.

1215
01:52:05,966 --> 01:52:09,725
We will find them, my Bey. Let's keep going.

1216
01:52:12,766 --> 01:52:15,285
Bala. Bala.

1217
01:52:15,526 --> 01:52:17,965
I feel cold, Osman.

1218
01:52:21,566 --> 01:52:23,325
This...

1219
01:52:24,006 --> 01:52:27,125
What is this? Poison's effect..

1220
01:52:27,326 --> 01:52:28,965
...is getting stronger.

1221
01:52:29,806 --> 01:52:31,885
We can't do this here.

1222
01:52:32,046 --> 01:52:34,965
Cerkutay, find somewhere to have rest.

1223
01:52:35,126 --> 01:52:37,205
-Come on.
-Okay, my Bey.

1224
01:52:37,246 --> 01:52:40,245
So we can also hunt and regain strength.

1225
01:52:40,326 --> 01:52:41,765
Come on.

1226
01:52:45,446 --> 01:52:47,125
Bala.

1227
01:52:48,006 --> 01:52:50,845
Hold on, my gazelle-eyed woman.

1228
01:52:51,006 --> 01:52:53,925
As you're here with me, I will hold on.

1229
01:52:54,206 --> 01:52:57,645
Yes, I'm here for you.

1230
01:52:57,966 --> 01:52:59,605
I'm here.

1231
01:53:01,846 --> 01:53:03,605
Sister Ulgen!

1232
01:53:03,686 --> 01:53:06,285
-Sister Ulgen, Ghazi got sick!
-Ghazi!

1233
01:53:06,606 --> 01:53:08,925
-Come.
-Mother.

1234
01:53:12,646 --> 01:53:15,965
Sit here. Give him some tea! Sister!

1235
01:53:21,006 --> 01:53:25,045
Give it to me. Drink this, my dear.

1236
01:53:28,486 --> 01:53:29,765
Meryem.

1237
01:53:30,406 --> 01:53:32,725
Meryem isn't here.

1238
01:53:35,566 --> 01:53:37,245
I'll go find Meryem.

1239
01:53:38,646 --> 01:53:40,365
Ulgen.

1240
01:53:41,326 --> 01:53:42,805
Fatma Hatun.

1241
01:53:43,966 --> 01:53:47,005
You don't look well. Sit down.

1242
01:53:48,046 --> 01:53:50,005
I'm fine. I'm fine.

1243
01:53:50,206 --> 01:53:52,365
I'll go find Meryem.

1244
01:53:58,846 --> 01:54:00,685
Jesus Christ.

1245
01:54:02,166 --> 01:54:05,405
I didn't avenge my parents.

1246
01:54:06,486 --> 01:54:08,485
Don't let me die.

1247
01:54:09,086 --> 01:54:11,445
The poor seeks help.

1248
01:54:12,566 --> 01:54:15,565
Give me strength.

1249
01:54:21,446 --> 01:54:23,085
Mother.

1250
01:54:24,246 --> 01:54:25,925
Where are you?

1251
01:54:29,046 --> 01:54:31,325
Why don't you come, mother?

1252
01:54:34,206 --> 01:54:36,005
Meryem.

1253
01:54:41,846 --> 01:54:43,405
Meryem.

1254
01:54:44,886 --> 01:54:46,725
Are you alright?

1255
01:54:48,286 --> 01:54:49,645
I'm fine.

1256
01:54:50,086 --> 01:54:53,845
-Come.
-I will be alright.

1257
01:54:55,246 --> 01:54:57,805
Before I avenge my parents

1258
01:54:58,486 --> 01:55:00,245
..I won't die.

1259
01:55:01,926 --> 01:55:04,485
We boiled some centaury.

1260
01:55:05,606 --> 01:55:07,525
Come on.

1261
01:55:08,846 --> 01:55:11,325
You need to drink some, alright?

1262
01:55:12,326 --> 01:55:14,485
Let's go.

1263
01:55:19,206 --> 01:55:20,565
Fatma.

1264
01:55:27,806 --> 01:55:31,405
You are burning. You're burning.

1265
01:55:33,486 --> 01:55:35,445
I need to bring help.

1266
01:55:47,126 --> 01:55:49,885
Should I help you, Fatma?

1267
01:56:27,166 --> 01:56:29,365
He took Orhan captive, huh?

1268
01:56:29,686 --> 01:56:32,645
That means, Sofia

1269
01:56:34,286 --> 01:56:37,805
...that he is our ally.

1270
01:56:43,166 --> 01:56:45,805
Ulugan waits.

1271
01:57:35,126 --> 01:57:38,165
As I was so close to kill Osman,

1272
01:57:38,406 --> 01:57:41,205
...you brought us here.

1273
01:57:41,486 --> 01:57:43,645
I never share my preys.

1274
01:57:44,566 --> 01:57:50,125
And only I decide who dies here.

1275
01:57:53,086 --> 01:57:59,285
By looking at my clothes, don't confuse
me with those ordinary tribe beys, Ulugan.

1276
01:57:59,726 --> 01:58:03,565
You're talking to the commander of Rome.

1277
01:58:07,046 --> 01:58:09,245
What did you do to Osman?

1278
01:58:10,526 --> 01:58:13,165
He could barely walk.

1279
01:58:24,766 --> 01:58:26,885
You're a smart woman.

1280
01:58:27,166 --> 01:58:29,485
You know well what to ask.

1281
01:58:32,926 --> 01:58:35,005
Your eyes..

1282
01:58:36,966 --> 01:58:38,965
Your look..

1283
01:58:42,806 --> 01:58:44,605
...is like poison.

1284
01:58:47,486 --> 01:58:49,685
And I like poison.

1285
01:58:51,966 --> 01:58:55,525
I put poison all the wells in their tribe.

1286
01:59:02,326 --> 01:59:04,205
Poena..

1287
01:59:05,846 --> 01:59:10,765
My little vengeance angel.

1288
01:59:12,566 --> 01:59:14,965
Don't die, my little baby.

1289
01:59:17,566 --> 01:59:21,605
I hope you didn't drink the water.

1290
01:59:27,046 --> 01:59:29,085
Sofia.

1291
01:59:30,366 --> 01:59:32,045
What poison is it?

1292
01:59:33,846 --> 01:59:35,565
Is there an antidote?

1293
01:59:37,206 --> 01:59:42,245
It seems there is someone
precious to you in the tribe.

1294
01:59:42,686 --> 01:59:48,005
Give me the antidote, Ulugan.

1295
01:59:54,286 --> 02:00:00,405
To demand something from me,
you should do something I want first.

1296
02:00:01,806 --> 02:00:04,005
What do you want?

1297
02:00:13,006 --> 02:00:15,445
Help us, my Allah.

1298
02:00:17,286 --> 02:00:20,965
Come on, come on.

1299
02:00:22,406 --> 02:00:24,005
Gonca, Holofira.

1300
02:00:24,966 --> 02:00:26,845
Mash them quickly and boil.

1301
02:00:26,846 --> 02:00:29,205
If we do it together, it'll
be enough for everyone.

1302
02:00:29,206 --> 02:00:32,165
Come on, sisters! Come on!

1303
02:00:35,486 --> 02:00:39,885
Come here, my dear. You will be alright.

1304
02:00:39,926 --> 02:00:42,605
I will heal you. Don't worry.

1305
02:00:42,646 --> 02:00:45,965
-Alaaddin Bey. Alaaddin Bey.
-Meryem.

1306
02:00:46,246 --> 02:00:48,245
Alaaddin Bey, you should help.

1307
02:00:48,646 --> 02:00:51,285
-Fatma Hatun blacked out. What?

1308
02:00:52,206 --> 02:00:54,845
Take her to the healing house.

1309
02:00:54,966 --> 02:00:56,245
Take me to my sister.

1310
02:00:56,326 --> 02:00:59,805
-In my tent.
-Your tent? That one?

1311
02:01:00,046 --> 02:01:02,885
-You go check her.
-Fatma!

1312
02:01:07,566 --> 02:01:11,085
Fatma... Fatma,
you will be alright.

1313
02:01:11,246 --> 02:01:14,485
You will be alright, my
beautiful sister. My dear sister...

1314
02:01:15,406 --> 02:01:17,965
My dear...

1315
02:01:29,846 --> 02:01:32,085
Come on, alps!

1316
02:01:41,366 --> 02:01:43,845
I'm not helpless.

1317
02:01:44,606 --> 02:01:46,765
I'm on my own..

1318
02:01:47,206 --> 02:01:50,525
..but not helpless.

1319
02:01:56,526 --> 02:02:00,725
Meryem, Meryem.
You aren't well either.

1320
02:02:01,566 --> 02:02:04,285
Let's go to the healing house.

1321
02:02:04,406 --> 02:02:07,125
Let's go, Meryem.

1322
02:02:07,566 --> 02:02:11,045
You're being stubborn but you aren't well.

1323
02:02:12,086 --> 02:02:16,405
Help us, my Allah. Help us.

1324
02:02:47,246 --> 02:02:49,365
Bala.

1325
02:02:57,446 --> 02:03:01,685
-Bala.
-Osman.

1326
02:03:03,366 --> 02:03:05,685
You're burning in fever.

1327
02:03:06,246 --> 02:03:08,885
You're burning.

1328
02:03:13,846 --> 02:03:15,285
Open your mouth.

1329
02:03:15,366 --> 02:03:18,725
Take this. This will be good for you.

1330
02:03:19,326 --> 02:03:20,845
This..

1331
02:03:21,526 --> 02:03:24,485
...will decrease the poison's effect.

1332
02:03:31,126 --> 02:03:32,805
Osman.

1333
02:03:37,446 --> 02:03:41,125
How are people in the tribe doing?

1334
02:03:43,166 --> 02:03:48,525
Don't worry. Alaaddin
will definitely find the cure.

1335
02:03:49,366 --> 02:03:51,885
And we will endure, Bala.

1336
02:03:53,006 --> 02:03:55,045
For our children.

1337
02:03:58,846 --> 02:04:03,045
Look at me. When I see you like this,

1338
02:04:03,446 --> 02:04:06,645
...I remember the times you were sick.

1339
02:04:07,006 --> 02:04:10,525
You slept all the time first but then..

1340
02:04:10,846 --> 02:04:15,405
Look. I'm a strong woman, Brunet Osman.

1341
02:04:15,766 --> 02:04:21,605
A hatun walking in your
path won't fall down easily.

1342
02:04:21,726 --> 02:04:24,725
Of course, you are strong.

1343
02:04:25,086 --> 02:04:29,725
Behind every strong woman, there is a mountain.

1344
02:04:30,286 --> 02:04:32,125
I am your mountain.

1345
02:04:32,486 --> 02:04:35,645
I will never let anything happen to you.

1346
02:04:35,886 --> 02:04:40,045
Well... I'm getting better now.

1347
02:04:41,926 --> 02:04:44,085
But..

1348
02:04:44,606 --> 02:04:46,045
Orhan..

1349
02:04:46,526 --> 02:04:50,205
Knowing the enemy caught him...

1350
02:04:51,246 --> 02:04:53,165
..makes my heart ache.

1351
02:04:53,246 --> 02:04:56,165
Don't worry. Orhan is strong.

1352
02:04:56,206 --> 02:04:59,965
He has my blood. He won't die easily.

1353
02:05:00,126 --> 02:05:04,845
Besides, they have to kill me first.

1354
02:05:05,566 --> 02:05:09,325
Don't worry. We will beat this poison.

1355
02:05:09,886 --> 02:05:11,885
We will beat the enemy as well.

1356
02:05:12,006 --> 02:05:13,525
God willing.

1357
02:05:13,806 --> 02:05:19,325
I will fight to my last breath for
us, our children and our state!

1358
02:05:19,366 --> 02:05:20,965
You will see.

1359
02:05:21,766 --> 02:05:25,965
Come on. Get some sleep. You should rest.

1360
02:05:40,686 --> 02:05:42,725
My beautiful sister.

1361
02:05:43,846 --> 02:05:46,565
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

1362
02:05:47,566 --> 02:05:51,365
O Healer! O Healer! O Healer!

1363
02:05:55,246 --> 02:05:58,085
Heal her, my Allah.

1364
02:06:00,526 --> 02:06:04,045
Many have died since the morning.

1365
02:06:05,326 --> 02:06:07,325
All those children..

1366
02:06:08,686 --> 02:06:11,125
What if this cure doesn't work?

1367
02:06:11,686 --> 02:06:14,085
I will figure something out, Ulgen Hatun.

1368
02:06:19,246 --> 02:06:22,005
Guldane, drink some.

1369
02:06:32,766 --> 02:06:34,605
I am...

1370
02:06:35,646 --> 02:06:37,445
What?

1371
02:06:37,726 --> 02:06:42,565
I did terrible things to you.

1372
02:06:45,366 --> 02:06:47,845
What do you mean, Guldane?

1373
02:06:48,646 --> 02:06:52,645
Begum... Begum Hatun..

1374
02:06:53,126 --> 02:06:56,525
...wanted to turn you two...

1375
02:06:58,526 --> 02:07:00,405
...against...

1376
02:07:01,806 --> 02:07:03,925
..each other.

1377
02:07:09,806 --> 02:07:12,005
I've brought clean water.

1378
02:07:19,726 --> 02:07:21,725
Don't tire yourself anymore.

1379
02:07:22,046 --> 02:07:25,605
We heard what you said.

1380
02:07:29,286 --> 02:07:31,605
Is she alright?

1381
02:07:38,566 --> 02:07:41,485
The medicine didn't heal anyone.

1382
02:07:50,486 --> 02:07:52,445
Alaaddin.

1383
02:07:52,926 --> 02:07:56,805
They are getting worse. What now?

1384
02:07:59,526 --> 02:08:01,685
We couldn't find sarsaparilla roots.

1385
02:08:01,726 --> 02:08:06,245
I thought this would decrease
the poison's effect, but it didn't.

1386
02:08:06,286 --> 02:08:08,245
It didn't.

1387
02:08:10,766 --> 02:08:12,965
Guldane.

1388
02:08:14,606 --> 02:08:17,485
Guldane! Guldane!

1389
02:08:18,606 --> 02:08:21,925
-My friend died!
-Wait, Begum Hatun.

1390
02:08:33,126 --> 02:08:35,725
She drank the medicine you made but she died.

1391
02:08:36,006 --> 02:08:40,365
-There is no cure for this?
-I will find. I will.

1392
02:08:40,886 --> 02:08:44,365
I will find the antidote whatever it takes!

1393
02:08:44,886 --> 02:08:46,605
Orhan.

1394
02:08:47,006 --> 02:08:50,205
Any news from Orhan, Osman?

1395
02:08:53,246 --> 02:08:56,405
Any news from Orhan?

1396
02:08:58,846 --> 02:09:01,805
Any news from Orhan?

1397
02:09:02,606 --> 02:09:05,885
Sleep, sleep. You should sleep.

1398
02:09:06,366 --> 02:09:08,485
Sleep.

1399
02:09:34,086 --> 02:09:35,965
My Allah.

1400
02:09:36,406 --> 02:09:41,605
Don't test me with my children, my Allah.

1401
02:09:42,046 --> 02:09:44,285
Please protect them.

1402
02:09:45,326 --> 02:09:49,805
It's You who gives and takes, my Allah.

1403
02:09:50,046 --> 02:09:56,525
You trusted us for them, my
Allah. Let me protect them.

1404
02:10:03,206 --> 02:10:07,125
My Halime... My precious...

1405
02:10:08,526 --> 02:10:10,685
I couldn't protect Halime.

1406
02:10:10,846 --> 02:10:16,445
Please protect my children, my Allah.

1407
02:10:30,966 --> 02:10:33,685
My Hatun, let me carry her.

1408
02:11:11,886 --> 02:11:14,285
Don't come, Osman.

1409
02:11:19,006 --> 02:11:21,045
Don't come.

1410
02:11:28,366 --> 02:11:31,565
Don't say that, Bala. No.

1411
02:11:36,086 --> 02:11:37,805
My daughter...

1412
02:11:37,886 --> 02:11:41,965
Look. Your father is here.

1413
02:11:42,686 --> 02:11:44,285
Wake up.

1414
02:11:50,446 --> 02:11:53,845
Wake up and hug your father.

1415
02:11:56,166 --> 02:11:58,285
Play games with him.

1416
02:11:58,526 --> 02:12:01,045
Come on.

1417
02:12:03,566 --> 02:12:06,445
Come on, my daughter.

1418
02:12:08,766 --> 02:12:10,965
Come on.

1419
02:12:11,966 --> 02:12:14,965
Bala... No.

1420
02:12:17,766 --> 02:12:19,685
Halime...

1421
02:12:41,486 --> 02:12:44,565
Don't upset your father.

1422
02:13:12,086 --> 02:13:14,285
Don't look, Osman Bey.

1423
02:13:15,206 --> 02:13:18,073
It's been ten days since
she fell into the river.

1424
02:13:18,085 --> 02:13:19,045
No.

1425
02:13:19,166 --> 02:13:21,085
No.

1426
02:14:02,286 --> 02:14:06,165
"To Allah we belong and to Him we will return."

1427
02:14:40,086 --> 02:14:41,365
My daughter...

1428
02:14:45,646 --> 02:14:47,685
Halime...

1429
02:14:55,406 --> 02:14:56,485
Osman..

1430
02:15:11,566 --> 02:15:13,045
I couldn't protect her...

1431
02:15:13,806 --> 02:15:17,765
I couldn't protect her Osman... I left her...

1432
02:15:17,926 --> 02:15:19,485
I left her there..

1433
02:15:19,486 --> 02:15:21,245
I couldn't hold her hand!

1434
02:15:22,446 --> 02:15:24,485
I couldn't hold her hand!

1435
02:15:24,486 --> 02:15:28,245
I left her there!

1436
02:15:28,246 --> 02:15:30,045
I couldn't protect my daughter!

1437
02:15:30,046 --> 02:15:33,645
I couldn't protect my child

1438
02:15:38,806 --> 02:15:41,605
I left her...

1439
02:15:41,606 --> 02:15:44,645
I left her there!

1440
02:15:51,966 --> 02:15:55,005
Can I come in, my Bey?

1441
02:15:55,966 --> 02:15:59,805
Cerkutay... Come in, Cerkutay!

1442
02:16:05,126 --> 02:16:06,845
Ilbay found the tracks, my Bey.

1443
02:16:06,846 --> 02:16:08,765
Good, then...

1444
02:16:08,766 --> 02:16:11,205
We'll perform our morning prayer and leave.

1445
02:16:11,206 --> 02:16:13,205
Thanks to Allah.

1446
02:16:13,246 --> 02:16:15,565
Bala, you go to the tribe now.

1447
02:16:15,566 --> 02:16:17,765
We don't know what our children are doing.

1448
02:16:18,046 --> 02:16:21,685
As you order, my Bey. -My Bey...

1449
02:16:22,886 --> 02:16:24,365
You are not alright..

1450
02:16:24,366 --> 02:16:26,085
Orhan and Boran..

1451
02:16:26,326 --> 02:16:27,805
We will save them.

1452
02:16:27,806 --> 02:16:30,045
As you order my Bey.

1453
02:16:56,686 --> 02:16:58,525
No, my Bey! No!

1454
02:16:58,526 --> 02:17:03,205
The tracks disappear after a point!

1455
02:17:05,004 --> 02:17:06,205
What?

1456
02:17:07,446 --> 02:17:08,885
We won't stop.

1457
02:17:09,486 --> 02:17:12,763
We'll keep looking. Until we find Orhan...

1458
02:17:13,446 --> 02:17:16,965
...we will not stop. Come on.

1459
02:17:17,726 --> 02:17:20,683
My Bey.. My Bey...

1460
02:17:21,245 --> 02:17:23,045
The poison flows in our blood.

1461
02:17:23,046 --> 02:17:26,805
At least you should go to the
tribe, and I'll keep searching.

1462
02:17:26,806 --> 02:17:31,565
What are you saying? No.

1463
02:17:37,406 --> 02:17:40,525
This is the rope that
will pull you into the well.

1464
02:17:41,126 --> 02:17:42,205
My Bey.

1465
02:17:42,846 --> 02:17:44,205
There are tracks here!

1466
02:17:45,165 --> 02:17:47,924
Let me go.

1467
02:18:17,004 --> 02:18:18,843
Dastard dogs.

1468
02:18:19,084 --> 02:18:20,885
They covered it with leaves.

1469
02:18:24,206 --> 02:18:26,004
Tracks go this way.

1470
02:18:29,566 --> 02:18:31,405
Dastard dog.

1471
02:18:32,084 --> 02:18:33,843
This way.

1472
02:18:34,446 --> 02:18:36,205
Come on.

1473
02:18:36,886 --> 02:18:39,885
This way.

1474
02:18:51,046 --> 02:18:52,683
Commander Ulugan.

1475
02:18:52,886 --> 02:18:57,485
Is the trap that will bring Osman to us ready?

1476
02:18:57,486 --> 02:19:00,525
-It is ready, commander.
-Is the bait ready?

1477
02:19:01,046 --> 02:19:02,924
It's ready too, commander.

1478
02:19:09,846 --> 02:19:11,125
Come Osman.

1479
02:19:12,004 --> 02:19:14,924
Spread your wings and come to your death.

1480
02:19:27,126 --> 02:19:29,045
Mother...

1481
02:19:38,846 --> 02:19:39,885
Mother...

1482
02:19:41,606 --> 02:19:43,683
Is there news from Orhan?

1483
02:19:43,726 --> 02:19:46,965
We found their tracks, they
are after them my daughter.

1484
02:19:46,966 --> 02:19:49,725
God willing they will find him.
-God willing.

1485
02:19:49,726 --> 02:19:52,045
Are you alright?

1486
02:19:52,046 --> 02:19:55,165
What... what happened here?

1487
02:19:56,366 --> 02:19:59,645
Mother, they poisoned the water.

1488
02:20:01,286 --> 02:20:05,205
Alaeddin is searching for the
antidote, but he hasn't found it yet.

1489
02:20:06,966 --> 02:20:09,645
What about you and Osman Bey? Are you alright?

1490
02:20:09,646 --> 02:20:13,365
You drank the water too.
-We are alright.

1491
02:20:14,166 --> 02:20:15,605
Where is Fatma?

1492
02:20:18,606 --> 02:20:20,365
Fatma is poisoned, mother.

1493
02:20:20,366 --> 02:20:21,965
We took her to the tent.

1494
02:20:22,286 --> 02:20:26,125
You take care of our people,
I will go and check Fatma.

1495
02:20:27,366 --> 02:20:30,925
Meryem?
-She is with Fatma. -Good.

1496
02:20:42,406 --> 02:20:44,645
Mother...

1497
02:20:44,646 --> 02:20:49,325
Let me go...

1498
02:20:52,966 --> 02:20:56,005
Mother.

1499
02:20:57,806 --> 02:21:00,325
Mother..

1500
02:21:01,366 --> 02:21:03,965
Mother...

1501
02:21:04,486 --> 02:21:06,325
Mother...

1502
02:21:11,526 --> 02:21:12,925
My Fatma!

1503
02:21:13,926 --> 02:21:15,645
Mother..

1504
02:21:16,286 --> 02:21:17,765
My daughter?

1505
02:21:26,486 --> 02:21:27,645
My daughter!

1506
02:21:47,566 --> 02:21:52,085
My Bey, are you alright?
-I am, I am alright, Cerkutay.

1507
02:21:52,966 --> 02:21:54,645
What is the situation?

1508
02:21:54,646 --> 02:21:58,525
These nokers are positioned on
the right side of this den of dogs.

1509
02:21:58,686 --> 02:22:02,423
They are all waiting around
that Ulugan dog's tent.

1510
02:22:02,435 --> 02:22:03,685
Orhan and Boran?

1511
02:22:10,926 --> 02:22:11,965
My Bey.

1512
02:22:11,966 --> 02:22:14,485
What's the situation on the left side, Ilbay?

1513
02:22:14,486 --> 02:22:16,325
My Bey, I saw them.

1514
02:22:16,326 --> 02:22:18,525
They are there, in the headquarters.

1515
02:22:19,286 --> 02:22:20,525
What about the nokers?

1516
02:22:20,526 --> 02:22:22,765
My Bey, there are patrolling soldiers.

1517
02:22:22,846 --> 02:22:24,565
But the measures are not strict.

1518
02:22:24,726 --> 02:22:26,925
Apparently, they think we won't find them.

1519
02:22:27,206 --> 02:22:29,845
Go ahead.

1520
02:22:49,366 --> 02:22:50,805
They are there, my Bey.

1521
02:22:53,086 --> 02:22:55,845
Ilbay, you will go from the left.

1522
02:22:55,846 --> 02:22:59,085
Cerkutay, you from the
right. Handle the guard too.

1523
02:22:59,086 --> 02:23:01,925
As you order my Bey.

1524
02:23:46,766 --> 02:23:48,765
Orhan.

1525
02:23:51,446 --> 02:23:55,005
Boran, brother! I am here brother!

1526
02:23:59,726 --> 02:24:01,845
My Bey... -Boran

1527
02:24:02,886 --> 02:24:03,925
My Bey...

1528
02:24:04,806 --> 02:24:06,205
We are trapped.

1529
02:24:08,326 --> 02:24:10,525
My Bey.

1530
02:24:22,726 --> 02:24:24,765
Welcome Osman..

1531
02:24:27,126 --> 02:24:30,045
Dastard dog..

1532
02:24:39,846 --> 02:24:42,885
Faithless dog...

1533
02:24:44,326 --> 02:24:49,085
You came for your son and your
Alp, but you are at the end of the road.